1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	0				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	Kaz, what kind of shape is that plant the\n"professor" gave us in?\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	1				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	First time I laid eyes on it, I thought it was some\nkind of joke.\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	2				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	It was a giant birdhouse - seagulls everywhere.\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	3				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	We eventually scraped off most of the rust and\nbird crap.\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	4				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	The underlying structure's intact - a little elbow\ngrease and we should be in business.\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	5				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	Who used to own it, anyway?\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	6				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	Whatever shape it's in now, somebody sank some\nserious money into building it.\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	7				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	From what I can tell, an American university built it\nas a research platform\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	8				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	for ocean thermal energy conversion, "OTEC."\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	9				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	The name's still on some of the rusty old power\nturbines.\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	10				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	I'm guessing they must have had government and\ncorporate assistance to build it, too.\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	11				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	But they couldn't solve the thermal efficiency\nproblem, and the project was canceled.\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	12				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	Then after the university abandoned it,\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	13				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	a KGB front company scooped it up for next to\nnothing... At least, that's my theory.\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	14				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	How'd the KGB manage to buy a plant built with\nAmerican capital, front company or not?\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	15				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	Yeah, that "professor" is quite the operator.\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	16				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	One other thing:\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	17				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	the plant's set up so that it can join up with other\nplants of the same standard.\n
1	en	148	0x944b0	37963	18				v_bri_kaz0010_000_0	22	So they were originally planning on expanding the\nplace, huh?\n
