1	en	148	0x94d00	38096	6				v_bri_kaz0010_010_0	7	Appreciate it, Boss.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	0				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Snake, you can use the Fulton Surface-to-air\nRecovery System\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	1				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	to send prisoners and unconscious mercenaries\nyou encounter back to the Mother Base.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	2				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	I know you've used the Fulton before,\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	3				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	but just to make sure I'm not missing anything,\nlet's review the steps.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	4				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	OK.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	5				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	First, attach a balloon to the unconscious enemy\nor captured prisoner.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	6				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Right. I hook a wire to the their waist, and on the\nother end of the wire there's a helium balloon.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	7				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Right. Then we'll send over a chopper to catch the\nfloating balloon with its recovery hook and reel it\nup into its cargo hold.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	8				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	And that's it.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	9				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	And that's it. We finished installing the recovery\nhook on the Huey...\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	10				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Wait, Kaz, something doesn't make sense about this\nwhole process.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	11				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Not this again...\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	12				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Normally, Fulton recovery is for when you're using\nfixed-wing aircraft.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	13				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	With a helicopter, isn't it simpler to land and pick\nup directly?\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	14				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Listen, Snake, you're gonna be calling for\nrecoveries repeatedly throughout your mission.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	15				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	We want to keep the risk of taking enemy fire to a\nminimum.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	16				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	The best way to get that done that is to do the\nrecovery in a high-speed fly-by.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	17				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	That's what the Fulton Surface-to-air Recovery\nSystem is for.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	18				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Uh huh... what's the real reason?\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	19				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Helicopters are cheaper.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	20				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	And the repair bills will start adding up once the\nbullets start flying...\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	21				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Thought so. Kaz, I know we need to keep costs\ndown, but...\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	22				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Boss, you really need to get rid of this whole Army\nmentality. We're not the Pentagon.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	23				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	We don't have billions of taxpayer dollars to play\nwith. And besides...\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	24				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Fine, fine. Just pick a reason that makes sense.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	25				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Helicopters have quicker response time. Sounds\nstrange, yeah, but it works great, I promise.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	26				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	You'll get used to it before long.\n
1	en	149	0x95220	38178	27				v_bri_kaz0030_000_0	28	Yeah, I hope so.\n
1	en	149	0x95c80	38344	0	501	2089	0x0e463a34	v_bri_kaz0060_000_0	11	Remember why we created MSF, Snake: to provide\nmilitary force to whoever needs it,\n
