1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	0					26	Life's funny sometimes, isn't it?\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	1					26	What brought that on?\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	2					26	We first met as enemies on the battlefield, and\nnow here we are fighting side by side.\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	3					26	You mean Colombia?\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	4					26	Yeah. After I quit the JSDF, I made my way there\nand got myself a position\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	5					26	as a drill sergeant for a band of revolutionaries,\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	6					26	despite the fact that I'd never seen a day of\ncombat.\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	7					26	I see you had the gift for talking business in\nSpanish even back then.\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	8					26	C'mon, stop it, you're making me blush.\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	9					26	Unlucky for me, though, you were in the service of\nthe Colombian Army.\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	10					26	I remember it like it was yesterday. It all happened\nin an instant.\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	11					26	You guys ambushed us, and half my unit was taken\nout.\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	12					26	My mind went totally blank. I couldn't keep it\ntogether... My whole unit was wiped out...\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	13					26	and I was left half-dead from a bomb blast.\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	14					26	Then, as I was leaving, you yelled out at me...\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	15					26	"I came all the way from Japan to be here. My\nplace is on the battlefield."\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	16					26	Then you asked for my help, saying, "I want to be\nthe one to end it."\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	17					26	I remember being surprised that there were still\nsamurai in Japan.\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	18					26	You guys came over to me. I had a grenade hidden\nunder me.\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	19					26	But even then you were too fast. The second I\npulled the pin,\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	20					26	you grabbed the hand I was using to hold the\ngrenade with both palms.\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	21					26	I didn't want it to go off. I'd heard samurai were a\nproud bunch. I wanted to know\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	22					26	why one of them would stoop so low as to try and\ntake his opponent with him.\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	23					26	And I said, "I'll never lose again... We'll never lose\nagain."\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	24					26	Yeah. "We'll do whatever it takes, but we'll never be\nbeaten again."\n
1	en	163	0xa3900	41872	25					26	Then I passed out from the blood loss.\n
