1	en	166	0xa63e0	42558	7	6896	7718	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0	15	because you used to run around with your shirt\noff. Is that true?\n
1	en	166	0xa63e0	42558	8	7718	8526	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0	15	Don't believe everything you hear. They called me\n"Naked"\n
1	en	166	0xa63e0	42558	9	8526	9919	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0	15	because I went in without gear or food. I had to\nprocure everything on site...\n
1	en	166	0xa63e0	42558	10	9933	10964	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0	15	You mean they sent you into the jungle without\neven a pair of pants?!\n
1	en	166	0xa63e0	42558	11	11020	12483	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0	15	On a HALO jump from 35,000 feet?! Sweet Jesus,\nyou are a legend!!\n
1	en	166	0xa63e0	42558	12	12483	13207	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0	15	...You're busting my balls, aren't you, Kaz?\n
1	en	166	0xa63e0	42558	13	13249	13653	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0	15	A little bit, yeah.\n
1	en	166	0xa63e0	42558	14	13667	14099	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0	15	...Hilarious\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	0	445	1393	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	COoperative OPerationS, or CO-OPS for short,\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	1	1421	2452	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	is the term for taking on missions in teams of two\nor more.\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	2	2479	3260	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	The basic CO-OPS unit is a two-man cell.\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	3	3287	4304	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	Even a single teammate is great to have in enemy\nterritory.\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	4	4318	5308	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	And there are actually quite a few things you can't\ndo by yourself.\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	5	5335	6311	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	You can help each other climb walls, divide up\nmission roles...\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	6	6394	7634	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	On the other hand, if one of you is spotted, the\nother one's screwed, too.\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	7	7648	8665	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	And it's kind of tough for two people to hide in one\nsmall space.\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	8	8679	9626	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	Good point. But what's more important than\nanything\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	9	9626	10309	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	is how close you are to your comrades.\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	10	10309	11674	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	Well said. Working as a two-man cell can make the\nmission easier or harder\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	11	11674	12357	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	depending on how well you work together.\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	12	12427	13569	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	It's also good to note that if you've got a clear,\nspecific objective,\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	13	13583	14558	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	it can be to your advantage to use an even bigger\nteam.\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	14	14600	16021	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	That said, teams of three or more run a much\ngreater risk of being spotted.\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	15	16035	17303	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	Yeah. In a sneaking mission, the fewer people you\nhave,\n
1	en	166	0xa6910	42641	16	17303	17902	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0	17	the easier it is to get around.\n
