1	en	167	0xa7370	42807	0	445	1866	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0	10	Another thing - during a mission you can assume\nwhat we'll call the Snake Formation.\n
1	en	167	0xa7370	42807	1	1894	2995	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0	10	Same as your code name - but probably not\nstandard operating procedure\n
1	en	167	0xa7370	42807	2	2995	3845	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0	10	for a guy who specializes in going solo.\n
1	en	167	0xa7370	42807	3	3845	4904	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0	10	Damn right. There's only room for one Snake.\n
1	en	167	0xa7370	42807	4	4931	5851	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0	10	In CO-OPS, though, it's a highly effective formation.\n
1	en	167	0xa7370	42807	5	5851	6979	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0	10	The signal for Snake Formation is to tap your\nteammate on the shoulder.\n
1	en	167	0xa7370	42807	6	7244	8512	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0	10	Can't form up until you're close enough to reach\nout and touch someone.\n
1	en	167	0xa7370	42807	7	8526	9501	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0	10	Entering Snake Formation is called going "Snake In."\n
1	en	167	0xa7370	42807	8	9529	10755	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0	10	When you're Snake In, the soldier at the front of\nthe line controls movement.\n
1	en	167	0xa7370	42807	9	10797	11842	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0	10	The soldiers in back focus on scouting and attack.\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	0	445	1448	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	Just because your heart stops doesn't mean you're\ndead immediately.\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	1	1476	2521	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	Right. The heart just circulates blood through the\nbody.\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	2	2549	4221	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	But stopping it does cut oxygen supply to the\nbrain - you'll be dead soon after.\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	3	4249	4862	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	Which is why we have CPR.\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	4	4904	5419	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	Let's say your heart does stop.\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	5	5419	6770	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	If someone performs CPR before your brain cells\ndie you can recover.\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	6	6826	7871	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	In CO-OPS, when the LIFE Gauge drops to zero,\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	7	7871	8498	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	it means you're in a near-death state.\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	8	8498	9250	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	You won't be able to move or anything else.\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	9	9264	10574	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	Performing CPR on near-death teammates can\nbring them back into action.\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	10	10616	11828	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	Of course, performing CPR in the middle of battle\nisn't exactly safe.\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	11	11842	12427	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	You're leaving yourself exposed.\n
1	en	167	0xa7780	42872	12	12455	13820	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0	18	Even so, in CO-OPS you and your teammates are\nall in the same boat.\n
