1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	0				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	In CO-OPS, maintaining close communications with\nyour teammates is crucial.\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	1				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	Absolutely. Losing track of each other on the\nbattlefield is a good way\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	2				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	for a unit to get itself wiped out.\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	3				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	Enemy positions. Orders. Distress calls.\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	4				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	When communications break down, you get picked\noff one by one.\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	5				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	Now, about CO-OPS Comms.\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	6				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	CO-OPS Comms…\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	7				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	It's a radio system for communicating with CO-OPS\nteammates.\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	8				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	First open the menu, then select "CO-OPS Comms."\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	9				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	After that, press one button to choose a category,\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	10				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	then another button to select the actual message.\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	11				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	So basically you use different combinations of two\nbuttons\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	12				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	to send different messages.\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	13				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	Easy enough.\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	14				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	You can set which messages go with which\nbuttons during mission prep.\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	15				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	Sounds like it's going to be a pain to send\nmessages until I get used to it.\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	16				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	Then why don't you assign CO-OPS Comms to\nwhatever button you like?\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	17				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	That should make things a little quicker and easier.\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	18				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	Just go to "Key Config".\n
1	en	169	0xa9240	43300	19				v_bri_mis_kaz0130_000_0	20	I'll give it a try.\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	0	473	1588	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	Snake, you familiar with the Japanese word\n"kotodama"?\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	1	1880	2368	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	Kotodama...?\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	2	2382	3329	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	Unfortunately, there's no direct equivalent in\nEnglish...\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	3	3329	4458	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	But to keep it simple, let's call it a sort of "Battle\nCry."\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	4	4527	5029	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	"Battle Cry," huh?\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	5	5071	6436	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	Right. But, Kotodama is actually a deep Japanese\nconcept.\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	6	6561	7565	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	"Koto" means word, and "dama" means spirit.\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	7	7578	8791	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	It signifies that words have power that affect our\nreality...\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	8	9306	10128	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	Ah... You feeling OK?\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	9	10128	11103	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	Guess I made it sound kind of like mumbo-jumbo,\nhuh.\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	10	11229	12580	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	Seriously, though, haven't you ever felt energized\nwhen a teammate cheered you on?\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	11	12580	14168	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	Or - the other way around - ever had your legs cut\nout from under you by a thoughtless remark?\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	12	14349	15645	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	I know the feeling. Words can have a powerful\nmental effect on people.\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	13	15659	16272	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	Same goes for CO-OPS Comms.\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	14	16300	17359	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	Offering praise to somebody could make them run\nfaster than usual.\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	15	17373	18822	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	Or make somebody who thinks they're done for get\nup and fight again... See what I'm saying?\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	16	18822	19825	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	I get the picture. So it works in reverse, too.\n
1	en	169	0xa98c0	43404	17	19853	21329	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1	18	The powers of words are many and varied. Try\nusing them for yourself.\n
