1	en	170	0xaa690	43625	0				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_010_1	11	Up to two people can fit inside a cardboard box.\n
1	en	170	0xaa690	43625	1				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_010_1	11	Tell me how!\n
1	en	170	0xaa690	43625	2				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_010_1	11	Move close to a box with a teammate inside and\nan Icon will appear.\n
1	en	170	0xaa690	43625	3				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_010_1	11	Then press <I=ACT>.\n
1	en	170	0xaa690	43625	4				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_010_1	11	You'll stay inside as long as <I=ACT> is pressed.\n
1	en	170	0xaa690	43625	5				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_010_1	11	So... Same as Snake Formation, huh.\n
1	en	170	0xaa690	43625	6				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_010_1	11	Exactly the same. In fact, when you put on a\ncardboard box when Snake In,\n
1	en	170	0xaa690	43625	7				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_010_1	11	both of you can climb inside.\n
1	en	170	0xaa690	43625	8				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_010_1	11	A box big enough to hold me and my buddy...\n
1	en	170	0xaa690	43625	9				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_010_1	11	These are fine times we live in, eh, Kaz?\n
1	en	170	0xaa690	43625	10				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_010_1	11	Yyyyeah, sure, Boss...\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	0				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	Snake, the R&D team came up with something new...\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	1				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	What is this?!\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	2				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	It's a cardboard tank. It's got enough room for two\npeople,\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	3				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	same as any other cardboard box.\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	4				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	Apparently the guy in front drives, and the guy in\nback is the gunner...\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	5				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	Hold on. Kaz, who the hell came up this thing?!\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	6				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	I'm sorry, Boss. He meant well, I swear.\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	7				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	I know it's nowhere near as good as a real tank,\nbut still...\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	8				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	It's BRILLIANT!!\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	9				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	Huh?\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	10				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	The perfect synthesis of stealth and attack power.\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	11				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	Compact, elegant design. The finest example of a\nweapon I've ever seen!\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	12				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	Seriously, Kaz, I need to meet the guy who made\nthis. I wanna shake his hand.\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	13				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	Y-you're serious? Snake, look at it, it's...\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	14				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	It's a masterpiece, in every sense of the word. You\ndon't agree?\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	15				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	N-no, I...!\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	16				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	Ooh, what's that? A tank? I like it!\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	17				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	Paz?!\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	18				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	I hate tanks, but this one I think I could get used\nto.\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	19				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	I love that it's a zero emissions vehicle - it will not\nhurt the forests of Costa Rica.\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	20				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	What?!\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	21				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	Nice work, Kaz. I see I made the right choice\nmaking you second in command.\n
1	en	170	0xaaa10	43681	22				v_bri_mis_kaz0140_030_0	23	But I... Is there something wrong with me?!\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	0				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	Snake, about that cassette player Gálvez was\ncarrying...\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	1				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	What about it?\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	2				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	That was no Russian imitation.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	3				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	It was the real deal - a prototype developed by a\nJapanese company.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	4				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	Get out of here!\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	5				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	It's true. It had the Sony logo on it. The product\nname is "WALKMAN."\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	6				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	WALKMAN...\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	7				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	It's a revolutionary new concept. Music you can\nlisten to on the go.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	8				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	You can take with you when you leave the house.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	9				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	I gave it a listen,\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	10				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	and you wouldn't believe how good the sound\nquality is for something so tiny.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	11				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	And in stereo, too. Think of the technology that\nmust have gone into it.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	12				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	And that tape is equally amazing.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	13				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	The treble range is clearly superior to any other\ncassette ever made. Stylish, too.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	14				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	How'd Gálvez get his hands on a model that's not\neven out yet?\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	15				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	Beats me. It's not the kind of thing I'd expect some\nstodgy Soviet to be into.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	16				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	Me neither. Tell you what, though, it's a fine piece\nof work.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	17				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	It'd let me listen to my music when I want, where I\nwant.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	18				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	I... never thought I'd hear you say that. But I have\nto agree.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	19				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	Me, I'm a recording freak,\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	20				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	and I always used to laugh at the idea of a\nportable player.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	21				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	But now that I've seen it in action, I've changed my\nmind.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	22				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	Being able to take your music with you...\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	23				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	This could be the start of a revolution in music.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	24				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	Could be.\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	25				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	I'm having the guys at Mother Base study and\nanalyze it. Who knows?\n
1	en	171	0xab160	43798	26				v_bri_mis_kaz0150_000_0	27	They might be able to come up with something\neven better.\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	0	445	1421	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	Going by this map, you've got a lot of different\nterrain types between\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	1	1421	2396	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	you and the hut where the Sandinista\ncomandante's being held.\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	2	2674	3566	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	Looks that way, doesn't it. Starting with jungle.\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	3	3580	4304	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	The enemy won't be able to see you very well,\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	4	4318	5433	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	but your visibility won't be so hot, either. Stay alert.\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	5	5489	6213	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	Next you've got the swamps along the river.\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	6	6255	7537	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	Make sure you get a good feel for how robust\nsurveillance is before diving in.\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	7	7565	7857	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	Will do.\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	8	7941	9292	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	Finally, there's the boat repair cabin - the\ncomandante's in there.\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	9	9362	10421	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	It's a key enemy outpost, and security is going to\nbe tight.\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	10	10448	11270	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	You may have to let brute force do the talking.\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	11	11312	11897	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	You still have a long way to go, Snake.\n
1	en	171	0xaba60	43942	12	11911	12928	0x0e463a34	v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0	13	Use caution, and don't make a racket out there.\nGot it?\n
