1	en	180	0xb43c0	46140	4	5489	6729	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0050_000_0	13	We study all these subjects and then use them to\nbuild the foundations of peace.\n
1	en	180	0xb43c0	46140	5	6798	8373	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_paz0050_000_0	13	Yeah, I get it... I'd just never heard the UN had a\nUniversity for Peace before.\n
1	en	180	0xb43c0	46140	6	8387	10685	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0050_000_0	13	Oh, that. Well, to be precise, it is still being set up.\nThey have started conducting research, but\n
1	en	180	0xb43c0	46140	7	10741	11563	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0050_000_0	13	the UN has not passed the necessary resolution\nyet.\n
1	en	180	0xb43c0	46140	8	11633	12260	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0050_000_0	13	Professor Gálvez couldn't wait that long...\n
1	en	180	0xb43c0	46140	9	12274	12928	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_paz0050_000_0	13	Oh, uh, right.\n
1	en	180	0xb43c0	46140	10	12942	13514	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0050_000_0	13	Costa Rica abolished its army,\n
1	en	180	0xb43c0	46140	11	13555	14586	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0050_000_0	13	and has also hosted the Central American Court of\nJustice.\n
1	en	180	0xb43c0	46140	12	14614	15993	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0050_000_0	13	It is the perfect place to build a university like\nours, don't you think?\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	0				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	Professor Gálvez was a KGB spy...?\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	1				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	I thought he helped me out of genuine concern for\nCosta Rica's future...\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	2				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	You didn't know?\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	3				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	How could I?! Believe me, Snake.\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	4				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	He introduced himself as a peace researcher at\nthe university.\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	5				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	He had an office and credentials and everything...\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	6				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	They're masters at creating cover personas. They\nthink of everything\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	7				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	- ID papers, jobs, sometimes even families.\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	8				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	Don't feel bad you didn't see through it.\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	9				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	But you did?\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	10				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	From the first time we met.\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	11				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	I wish you'd told me...\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	12				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	Sorry. I didn't know if it'd be right.\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	13				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	You might have gotten mixed up in things you\nshouldn't.\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	14				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	That is impressive, though. Sizing him up him at a\nsingle glance.\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	15				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	He reeked.\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	16				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	Reeked?\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	17				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	He had this unmistakable air about him...\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	18				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	The air of someone who's been given a mission\nand will see it through no matter what.\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	19				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	Like me. I could just smell it.\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	20				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	That is amazing, Snake!\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	21				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	Nah, I'm just kidding. It was his prosthetic hand.\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	22				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	Why would a professor from a peace university\nneed a tool for assassination?\n
1	en	180	0xb48c0	46220	23				v_bri_paz0190_000_0	24	...\n
1	en	181	0xb54b0	46411	0	473	1365	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_paz0070_000_1	10	Are there any large-scale ruins in Costa Rica, Paz?\n
1	en	181	0xb54b0	46411	1	1407	2410	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0070_000_1	10	There's a place east of Cartago called Guayabo.\n
1	en	181	0xb54b0	46411	2	2493	3232	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0070_000_1	10	They have ruins there, but they're not especially\nbig.\n
1	en	181	0xb54b0	46411	3	3650	4486	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_paz0070_000_1	10	Not the place I'm thinking of... Any others?\n
1	en	181	0xb54b0	46411	4	4527	5935	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0070_000_1	10	Well, if you go a little way across the border into\nNicaragua,\n
1	en	181	0xb54b0	46411	5	6004	8219	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0070_000_1	10	there's a place called La Fortaleza de la\nInmaculada Concepción. That's the only famous one.\n
1	en	181	0xb54b0	46411	6	8261	9195	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_paz0070_000_1	10	Then what were those ruins I saw from up on\nIrazu...?\n
1	en	181	0xb54b0	46411	7	9250	10783	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0070_000_1	10	There are a lot of things we still do not know\nabout Costa Rica's ancient civilizations.\n
1	en	181	0xb54b0	46411	8	10839	11730	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0070_000_1	10	There are giant stone spheres throughout the\ncountry.\n
1	en	181	0xb54b0	46411	9	11814	12719	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0070_000_1	10	What they were used for is still a mystery.\n
1	en	181	0xb58a0	46474	0				v_bri_paz0080_000_1	8	Paz, you said Costa Rica has no army, right?\n
1	en	181	0xb58a0	46474	1				v_bri_paz0080_000_1	8	Correct. Article 12 of the constitution declared\n
1	en	181	0xb58a0	46474	2				v_bri_paz0080_000_1	8	that the army as a permanent institution is\nabolished.\n
1	en	181	0xb58a0	46474	3				v_bri_paz0080_000_1	8	It does permit us to organize armed forces for\nnational defense\n
1	en	181	0xb58a0	46474	4				v_bri_paz0080_000_1	8	based on inter-American treaties.\n
1	en	181	0xb58a0	46474	5				v_bri_paz0080_000_1	8	Only temporarily, then.\n
1	en	181	0xb58a0	46474	6				v_bri_paz0080_000_1	8	In effect, yes. But in the years since the\nconstitution took effect,\n
1	en	181	0xb58a0	46474	7				v_bri_paz0080_000_1	8	Costa Rica has not once raised an army.\n
1	en	181	0xb5b70	46519	0					18	Paz. How does your country defend itself without\nan army?\n
1	en	181	0xb5b70	46519	1					18	Especially in a rough neighborhood like Central\nAmerica.\n
1	en	181	0xb5b70	46519	2					18	With the right kind of diplomacy.\n
1	en	181	0xb5b70	46519	3					18	If we live up to our ideals and earn the respect of\nother countries,\n
1	en	181	0xb5b70	46519	4					18	the international community will support us.\n
1	en	181	0xb5b70	46519	5					18	The two times Nicaragua actually did invade,\n
1	en	181	0xb5b70	46519	6					18	the conflict was resolved diplomatically under OAS\n(Organization of American States) auspices.\n
1	en	181	0xb5b70	46519	7					18	Doesn't that leave you depending on the U.S. after\nall?\n
1	en	181	0xb5b70	46519	8					18	American influence is unmatched, it is true.\n
