1	en	182	0xb62e0	46638	0	473	1783	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0090_000_0	10	The army was abolished 25 years ago, the year\nafter the civil war.\n
1	en	182	0xb62e0	46638	1	1894	2869	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0090_000_0	10	I learned about the sorrow of civil war from a very\nyoung age.\n
1	en	182	0xb62e0	46638	2	2995	4165	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0090_000_0	10	The futility of countrymen fighting each other, and\nthe tragedy...\n
1	en	182	0xb62e0	46638	3	4291	5377	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0090_000_0	10	Costa Rica learned the hard way. That is why it\nabolished its army.\n
1	en	182	0xb62e0	46638	4	5489	6394	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0090_000_0	10	It decided to pour its efforts into education\ninstead.\n
1	en	182	0xb62e0	46638	5	6548	7272	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0090_000_0	10	"More teachers than soldiers" was the slogan.\n
1	en	182	0xb62e0	46638	6	7314	8080	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_paz0090_000_0	10	Education is essential, no question.\n
1	en	182	0xb62e0	46638	7	8247	9334	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_paz0090_000_0	10	Even Che used to teach reading and writing in\nbetween guerrilla campaigns.\n
1	en	182	0xb62e0	46638	8	9418	10644	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0090_000_0	10	Costa Rica was poor at the time. We didn't have\nmany resources.\n
1	en	182	0xb62e0	46638	9	10811	12246	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0090_000_0	10	I suppose we had to pick one or the other - the\nmilitary or the schools.\n
1	en	182	0xb66e0	46702	0				v_bri_paz0100_000_0	8	Kaz was telling me Japan has a peace constitution,\ntoo.\n
1	en	182	0xb66e0	46702	1				v_bri_paz0100_000_0	8	That is right. Apparently when Costa Rica was\ndrafting its constitution,\n
1	en	182	0xb66e0	46702	2				v_bri_paz0100_000_0	8	they looked to the Japanese as a model.\n
1	en	182	0xb66e0	46702	3				v_bri_paz0100_000_0	8	Only Japan's constitution renounces war itself.\n
1	en	182	0xb66e0	46702	4				v_bri_paz0100_000_0	8	Unlike Costa Rica.\n
1	en	182	0xb66e0	46702	5				v_bri_paz0100_000_0	8	But... Japan has a Self-Defense Force, right? That I\ndo not get.\n
1	en	182	0xb66e0	46702	6				v_bri_paz0100_000_0	8	I think I will ask Mr. Miller about it next time I see\nhim. He said he used to be in the JSDF.\n
1	en	182	0xb66e0	46702	7				v_bri_paz0100_000_0	8	You're a curious one, aren't you? Don't study too\nhard.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	0				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	What was that you were saying... "peace is not the\nnatural state of men"?\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	1				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	You said you learned it in school.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	2				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	That's right. They're the words of the German\nphilosopher Immanuel Kant.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	3				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	In 1795 he wrote a book titled "Perpetual Peace."\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	4				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	Kant argued that it's precisely because peace is\nunnatural\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	5				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	that we have to make it ourselves.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	6				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	How?\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	7				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	That's what his book is about. Is the concept\nstarting to sound interesting now?\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	8				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	Not really... I belong in a more natural world.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	9				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	Is that so...\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	10				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	...My grandparents died in the civil war.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	11				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	If only we'd been at peace, they wouldn't have lost\ntheir lives.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	12				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	You actually wish for war?\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	13				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	It's not like I want to hurt innocent civilians.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	14				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	But if someone attacks you, what are you\nsupposed to do?\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	15				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	A country needs the strength to defend itself.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	16				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	Otherwise it faces invasion, oppression, political\nsubjugation.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	17				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	If they'd simply stop using force to tangle with\neach other,\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	18				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	countries wouldn't need force to defend themselves.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	19				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	And how would you guarantee that?\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	20				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	I...\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	21				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	...Sorry. But you have to understand how the world\nworks\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	22				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	in order to protect the ones you love.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	23				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	That's not to say ideals aren't important, too. They\nare.\n
1	en	182	0xb6a00	46752	24				v_bri_paz0110_000_0	25	You are right, Snake... Thanks. Peace!\n
1	en	183	0xb71f0	46879	0				v_bri_paz0120_000_0	8	Costa Rica's forests are more diverse than you\nmight expect.\n
1	en	183	0xb71f0	46879	1				v_bri_paz0120_000_0	8	Not all of them are tropical rain forests.\n
1	en	183	0xb71f0	46879	2				v_bri_paz0120_000_0	8	Costa Rica is close to the Equator, it is true, but it\nis also very mountainous.\n
1	en	183	0xb71f0	46879	3				v_bri_paz0120_000_0	8	I see what you mean.\n
1	en	183	0xb71f0	46879	4				v_bri_paz0120_000_0	8	Go up 4,000 feet in elevation and the temperature\ndrops more than seven degrees.\n
1	en	183	0xb71f0	46879	5				v_bri_paz0120_000_0	8	There are basically three types of forests.\n
1	en	183	0xb71f0	46879	6				v_bri_paz0120_000_0	8	The lowlands are covered in tropical rain forests,\nthe highlands by tropical cloud forests.\n
1	en	183	0xb71f0	46879	7				v_bri_paz0120_000_0	8	And areas where there is a dry season have\ntropical dry forests.\n
1	en	183	0xb7530	46931	0	473	2034	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0120_010_0	9	The lowlands along the Caribbean coast are mostly\ncovered by hot, humid tropical rain forests.\n
1	en	183	0xb7530	46931	1	2131	2897	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0120_010_0	9	What most people envision when they think of\n"jungle."\n
1	en	183	0xb7530	46931	2	3009	4374	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0120_010_0	9	The closely packed trees spread their branches\nout at great heights to soak up the sun.\n
1	en	183	0xb7530	46931	3	4527	5530	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0120_010_0	9	Their shade makes it dark near the ground, so be\ncareful.\n
1	en	183	0xb7530	46931	4	5600	6757	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0120_010_0	9	Of course, with so little light few plants can grow\non the ground,\n
1	en	183	0xb7530	46931	5	6812	7439	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0120_010_0	9	so it might actually be easier to walk.\n
1	en	183	0xb7530	46931	6	7481	8791	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_paz0120_010_0	9	So even if you could photosynthesize, it wouldn't\ndo you any good.\n
1	en	183	0xb7530	46931	7	8860	9738	0x0e55d959	v_bri_paz0120_010_0	9	Photosynthesize? People cannot do that.\n
1	en	183	0xb7530	46931	8	10128	10602	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_paz0120_010_0	9	Most people, anyway.\n
1	en	183	0xb78c0	46988	0				v_bri_paz0120_030_0	7	Areas with a distinct dry season, like the Pacific\ncoast, have tropical dry forests.\n
1	en	183	0xb78c0	46988	1				v_bri_paz0120_030_0	7	During the dry season, the trees drop their leaves.\nIt gives you a clearer view,\n
1	en	183	0xb78c0	46988	2				v_bri_paz0120_030_0	7	but at the same time there are fewer places to\nhide, so be careful.\n
1	en	183	0xb78c0	46988	3				v_bri_paz0120_030_0	7	Sounds dull.\n
1	en	183	0xb78c0	46988	4				v_bri_paz0120_030_0	7	It is not, really. A lot of trees flower during the dry\nseason.\n
1	en	183	0xb78c0	46988	5				v_bri_paz0120_030_0	7	Including my favorite, the tabebuia.\n
1	en	183	0xb78c0	46988	6				v_bri_paz0120_030_0	7	It has these amazingly vivid yellow flowers.\n
1	en	183	0xb7b80	47032	0				v_bri_paz0120_020_0	8	The cloud forests cover the central mountainous\nregion of the country.\n
1	en	183	0xb7b80	47032	1				v_bri_paz0120_020_0	8	They're perpetually shrouded in fog. You get wet\njust standing there.\n
1	en	183	0xb7b80	47032	2				v_bri_paz0120_020_0	8	It is as if the entire forest is inside a cloud.\n
1	en	183	0xb7b80	47032	3				v_bri_paz0120_020_0	8	Must make for poor visibility.\n
1	en	183	0xb7b80	47032	4				v_bri_paz0120_020_0	8	It does. But beauty, too. It is like being lost in some\nmystical, green labyrinth.\n
1	en	183	0xb7b80	47032	5				v_bri_paz0120_020_0	8	...I'd rather not get lost if that's OK.\n
1	en	183	0xb7b80	47032	6				v_bri_paz0120_020_0	8	The forests are also home to lots of rare animals.\n
1	en	183	0xb7b80	47032	7				v_bri_paz0120_020_0	8	Especially brightly colored frogs. They like the\nhumidity.\n
1	en	183	0xb7ea0	47082	0					5	You know that butterfly painted on Peace Walker -\nany idea what that is?\n
