1	en	186	0xba530	47699	3	3928	4709	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0	10	We did our best to sneak in undetected, but...\n
1	en	186	0xba530	47699	4	4959	5544	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0	10	one of the guards spotted us, and we...\n
1	en	186	0xba530	47699	5	5572	5823	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0	10	What is it?\n
1	en	186	0xba530	47699	6	5837	6840	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0	10	...I'm sorry, you'll have to ask Professor Gálvez the\nrest.\n
1	en	186	0xba530	47699	7	6868	7718	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0	10	...It's OK. You've been through a lot.\n
1	en	186	0xba530	47699	8	7732	8735	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0	10	I am sorry, I... I just cannot...\n
1	en	186	0xba530	47699	9	8749	10031	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0	10	You did great, Paz. I won't let your efforts go\nwasted.\n
1	en	186	0xba8b0	47755	0				v_bri_mis_paz0040_000_0	7	This is a tropical rainforest, just like Bosque del\nAlba.\n
1	en	186	0xba8b0	47755	1				v_bri_mis_paz0040_000_0	7	The temperature and humidity can be brutal. El\nCenegal means "Place of Mud."\n
1	en	186	0xba8b0	47755	2				v_bri_mis_paz0040_000_0	7	Mud. Great. I'll watch my step.\n
1	en	186	0xba8b0	47755	3				v_bri_mis_paz0040_000_0	7	This area often gets flooded by the river.\n
1	en	186	0xba8b0	47755	4				v_bri_mis_paz0040_000_0	7	There are canals here and there carved out by the\nwater.\n
1	en	186	0xba8b0	47755	5				v_bri_mis_paz0040_000_0	7	Good places to hide.\n
1	en	186	0xba8b0	47755	6				v_bri_mis_paz0040_000_0	7	But they'll also make it harder for you to see. Be\ncareful, Snake.\n
1	en	186	0xbab50	47797	0	445	1212	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0	9	There should be a suspension bridge around there.\n
1	en	186	0xbab50	47797	1	1239	1713	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0	9	In lowlands like this?\n
1	en	186	0xbab50	47797	2	1769	2633	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0	9	The ground nearby is harder and higher than usual.\n
1	en	186	0xbab50	47797	3	2716	3594	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0	9	The river cut through it, eventually creating a\nvalley.\n
1	en	186	0xbab50	47797	4	3636	4597	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0	9	There might be another way to get across the\nriver somewhere.\n
1	en	186	0xbab50	47797	5	4597	5349	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0	9	I wouldn't want to run into someone on the bridge.\n
1	en	186	0xbab50	47797	6	5391	6687	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0	9	The valley tends to be misty, so you might not be\nable to see the water from up there.\n
1	en	186	0xbab50	47797	7	6770	7314	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0	9	Fall and it'll leave more than a bump.\n
1	en	186	0xbab50	47797	8	7356	7787	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0	9	I'll be careful.\n
1	en	186	0xbae80	47848	0				v_bri_mis_paz0060_000_0	5	When a river floods an area, the banks can\ncollapse, creating a marsh.\n
1	en	186	0xbae80	47848	1				v_bri_mis_paz0060_000_0	5	You see a lot of them around here.\n
1	en	186	0xbae80	47848	2				v_bri_mis_paz0060_000_0	5	I'll need to watch the noise my feet make in el\ncenegal.\n
1	en	186	0xbae80	47848	3				v_bri_mis_paz0060_000_0	5	There's a marsh on the other side of the river, too.\n
1	en	186	0xbae80	47848	4				v_bri_mis_paz0060_000_0	5	The suspension bridge will take you there.\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	0	445	1630	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	The river running through here is Río del Jade, or\n"the Jade River."\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	1	1657	2438	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	Jade? Are there minerals around here?\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	2	2452	3287	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	No, it refers to the color of the water.\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	3	3357	4040	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	You'll have to go to Guatemala for jade.\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	4	4096	5475	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	Hmm... Doesn't look all that pretty from where I'm\nstanding.\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	5	5517	6673	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	We're still in the rainy season, so the river's a little\nmuddy.\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	6	6715	7606	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	It'll return to normal once the dry season starts.\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	7	7648	8554	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	Rivers are an important means of transport around\nhere.\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	8	8609	9822	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	They're relatively calm, and there are plenty of\ncanals along the coast, too.\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	9	9863	10978	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	A boat'd be more than enough to transport some\ngood-sized cargo.\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	10	10978	11619	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	Like... a nuclear weapon?\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	11	11967	12887	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	We don't know enough yet. I'll keep looking.\n
1	en	187	0xbb080	47880	12	12914	13221	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0	13	Thank you, Snake.\n
1	en	187	0xbb510	47953	0	445	1727	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0	10	There's a lot of banana cultivation along Costa\nRica's Caribbean coast.\n
1	en	187	0xbb510	47953	1	1839	2702	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0	10	The area's dotted with banana plantations.\n
1	en	187	0xbb510	47953	2	2772	3524	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0	10	Bananas have been Costa Rica's main crop\n
1	en	187	0xbb510	47953	3	3538	4611	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0	10	since they were introduced from Panama in the\n19th century.\n
1	en	187	0xbb510	47953	4	4695	5447	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0	10	They bring in a fair amount of foreign currency.\n
1	en	187	0xbb510	47953	5	5503	6227	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0	10	A real fruta de oro, huh?\n
1	en	187	0xbb510	47953	6	6241	7453	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0	10	Si. But exporting all those bananas requires a ton\nof land.\n
1	en	187	0xbb510	47953	7	7537	8219	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0	10	Hence all the plantations.\n
1	en	187	0xbb510	47953	8	8261	9543	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0	10	Clearing all that forest just to grow bananas robs\nanimals of their habitats.\n
1	en	187	0xbb510	47953	9	9654	10546	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0	10	I do not know how good that is for Costa Rica in\nthe end.\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	0	459	1267	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	Panama disease was rampant here about 20 years\nago,\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	1	1393	2284	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	putting a lot of banana plantations out of business.\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	2	2354	2716	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	Panama disease?\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	3	2786	3413	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	It is caused by a type of fungus.\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	4	3524	4695	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	Apparently it killed off almost all the banana\nspecies that used to grow here.\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	5	4736	5154	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	How could that happen?\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	6	5224	5893	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	Cultivated bananas do not produce seeds.\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	7	5948	7481	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	You have to remove and transplant part of the\nstem yourself. You plant them in the fields.\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	8	7523	8233	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	So you've got acres of identical plants?\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	9	8275	9487	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	Si. When one plant is infected, the disease spreads\nquickly.\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	10	9599	10407	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	Species lacking genetic diversity become weak.\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	11	10504	11075	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	They grow different bananas today,\n
1	en	187	0xbb8b0	48011	12	11103	11981	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0	13	ones said to be resistant to Panama disease.\n
1	en	187	0xbbd10	48081	0				v_bri_mis_paz0100_000_0	6	Costa Rica has several active volcanoes, Irazú\nbeing one of them.\n
1	en	187	0xbbd10	48081	1				v_bri_mis_paz0100_000_0	6	That's where "Camino de Lava" comes from, huh?\n
1	en	187	0xbbd10	48081	2				v_bri_mis_paz0100_000_0	6	The tropical dry forests around here are quite\ndifferent from our rainforests.\n
1	en	187	0xbbd10	48081	3				v_bri_mis_paz0100_000_0	6	They lose their leaves in the dry season.\n
1	en	187	0xbbd10	48081	4				v_bri_mis_paz0100_000_0	6	Tropical forests are not all thick jungles. A few of\nthem even have cacti.\n
1	en	187	0xbbd10	48081	5				v_bri_mis_paz0100_000_0	6	Some of Costa Rica's greatest assets are its\ndiverse forests and natural landscapes.\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	0	445	1588	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	Aldea de los Despiertos means "Village of the\nAwake."\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	1	1936	2229	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	Weird name.\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	2	2270	3510	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	The area's littered with coffee fields and there's a\nfactory nearby.\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	3	3608	4569	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	The villagers are fans of coffee, so...\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	4	4806	6185	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	They don't get much sleep, huh? They've got a\nsense of humor all right.\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	5	6283	7397	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	I cannot believe they would take over a place like\nthis and use it as a prison.\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	6	7481	8763	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	It is unforgiveable. For both la CIA and the thugs\nthey employ.\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	7	8832	9557	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	All the villagers wanted was to live in peace.\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	8	9654	10490	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	What gives la CIA the right to crush them like\nthat?!\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	9	10560	11438	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	They don't care about anyone's rights but their\nown.\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	10	11674	12204	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	It's just the way some people are.\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	11	12260	12705	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	You really think so?\n
1	en	188	0xbc2a0	48170	12	12747	14015	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0	13	Don't worry. It just gives me the right to teach\nthem a lesson.\n
1	en	188	0xbc730	48243	0	445	2159	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0	11	La CIA has taken control of this coffee factory,\ntoo. All to produce its drugs...\n
1	en	188	0xbc730	48243	1	2215	3204	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0	11	It was famous once, for its fine beans.\n
1	en	188	0xbc730	48243	2	3482	4722	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0	11	Cafetal Aroma Encantado... "Enchanting Aroma,"\nhuh?\n
1	en	188	0xbc730	48243	3	4764	5823	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0	11	Si. Once we've thrown the mercenaries out of\nCosta Rica,\n
1	en	188	0xbc730	48243	4	5935	6701	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0	11	I know it will make wonderful coffee again.\n
1	en	188	0xbc730	48243	5	6743	7370	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0	11	And then you must come and try some, Snake.\n
1	en	188	0xbc730	48243	6	7370	9306	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0	11	Sounds great. I wouldn't mind a cuppa joe after all\nthis is over. Oh, wait...\n
1	en	188	0xbc730	48243	7	9334	9557	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0	11	What is wrong?\n
1	en	188	0xbc730	48243	8	9599	11215	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0	11	No, I... just remembered this guy I knew who wasn't\nbig on coffee. English.\n
1	en	188	0xbc730	48243	9	11354	12552	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0	11	"Get rid of that muddy water and get a cup of\nblack tea down your gob," he'd say.\n
1	en	188	0xbc730	48243	10	12552	13918	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0	11	Ha! That's too bad for him - it is delicious.\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	0	445	1727	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	As I said before, building railroads in Costa Rica\nwas a dangerous job.\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	1	1839	2883	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	A lot of men died, and sometimes they stopped\nwork altogether.\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	2	2967	4193	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	This is one of those places. They had to cut\nthrough steep terrain,\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	3	4207	5405	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	so when they finally made it through they just built\nthe rail terminal right there.\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	4	5447	5921	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	And that's why they named it...\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	5	46138	64136	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	El Cadalso... the Gallows. Charming.\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	6				v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	I'm surprised the construction money didn't dry up\nthe way things were going.\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	7				v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	Actually, it did. But the bananas helped complete it,\nso they say.\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	8				v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	You mean... the energy the workers got from\neating bananas?\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	9				v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	I suppose they do have plenty of vitamins and...\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	10				v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	No, no, no, I meant the money they got to finish it\ncame from exporting bananas.\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	11				v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	Oh...\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	12				v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	But one thing is for certain!\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	13				v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	The owners of the railroads expanded into the\nbanana trade\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	14				v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	after construction was completed.\n
1	en	188	0xbcb50	48309	15				v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0	16	That was the start of banana cultivation in Costa\nRica.\n
1	en	189	0xbd110	48401	0	459	1741	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0	9	Snake, to the north of the village is a bridge that\ncrosses a hydraulic pipe,\n
1	en	189	0xbd110	48401	1	1783	2549	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0	9	though normally the bridge is not used by people.\n
1	en	189	0xbd110	48401	2	2577	3942	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0	9	If you slip you'll fall straight to the bottom of the\nvalley. Be careful.\n
1	en	189	0xbd110	48401	3	4012	4500	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0	9	What's a channel doing here?\n
1	en	189	0xbd110	48401	4	4527	5642	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0	9	It is not for irrigation - they're hydroelectric pipes.\n
1	en	189	0xbd110	48401	5	5767	6534	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0	9	I wonder if they run into Irazú's crater lake.\n
1	en	189	0xbd110	48401	6	6617	7509	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0	9	Normally they would build a reservoir at the\nbottom of the valley,\n
1	en	189	0xbd110	48401	7	7551	8247	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0	9	but it was probably too dangerous.\n
1	en	189	0xbd110	48401	8	8373	9292	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0	9	Los Cantos means "Sword Peak."\n
1	en	189	0xbd460	48454	0	445	1476	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0	9	You should be able to see across the Irazú\nmountain range from there.\n
1	en	189	0xbd460	48454	1	1532	3078	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0	9	There are not as many big trees at that elevation,\nand you'll probably be well above the mist.\n
1	en	189	0xbd460	48454	2	3622	4193	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0	9	It'll be tough to hide up there.\n
1	en	189	0xbd460	48454	3	4221	5099	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0	9	You're not thinking about the scenery right now,\nare you?\n
1	en	189	0xbd460	48454	4	5154	5893	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0	9	Not while I'm surrounded by bad guys.\n
1	en	189	0xbd460	48454	5	5907	6617	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0	9	You should have seen it when the country was at\npeace.\n
1	en	189	0xbd460	48454	6	6729	7258	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0	9	I know you'd have been impressed.\n
1	en	189	0xbd460	48454	7	7314	8874	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0	9	Well, that'll be our reward for a successful mission.\nSound good?\n
1	en	189	0xbd460	48454	8	8902	9668	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0	9	Wonderful. Thank you, Snake.\n
1	en	189	0xbd7c0	48508	0	445	1309	0x0e55d959	v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0	12	...There is... an old fort around there.\n
1	en	189	0xbd7c0	48508	1	1309	2201	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0	12	What is it, Paz? You sound... upset.\n
