1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	0				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	The first Somoza was originally no more than the\ncommander of la Guardia.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	1				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	Ordinarily, a man of his station could never hope to\nbecome president.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	2				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	But the president at the time had no power to\nback him.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	3				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	The only one with the strength to oppose him was\nGeneral Sandino.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	4				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	....No. Better to say the General was the only one\nwho dared oppose him.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	5				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	There was nothing special about him.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	6				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	Above all, it takes a strong will to see justice done.\nThat is what he taught us.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	7				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	It's also what motivated Somoza to have him killed...\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	8				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	Yes. The rest was easy. He got rid of the\npresident, taking office in a sham election.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	9				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	And once he had power, he never gave it up.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	10				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	Talk about heavy-handed.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	11				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	He had the Americans backing him, that's why.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	12				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	They didn't want to hand over power to a\nrebellious general.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	13				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	Even so, it's hard to believe Washington would give\nits blessing to a guy like that.\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	14				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	The American President at the time put it this way:\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	15				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	"Somoza may be a son of a bitch, but he's our son\nof a bitch."\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	16				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	In other words, better a dog or los sapos (Somoza\nand counter-revolutionaries)\n
1	en	193	0xc16a0	49514	17				v_bri_amd0020_010_0	18	than an anti-US regime.\n
1	en	193	0xc1d60	49622	0					10	The Managua Earthquake struck two years ago,\nthe day before Christmas Eve.\n
1	en	193	0xc1d60	49622	1					10	Giant cracks opened up in the streets.\n
1	en	193	0xc1d60	49622	2					10	Sleeping children were crushed in collapsing\nhouses.\n
1	en	193	0xc1d60	49622	3					10	No chance to escape. No visit from Santa Claus.\n
1	en	193	0xc1d60	49622	4					10	Thanks to Somoza, the old houses could not even\nget rebuilt... It was a nightmare.\n
1	en	193	0xc1d60	49622	5					10	I heard the epicenter was right in the middle of the\ncity.\n
1	en	193	0xc1d60	49622	6					10	Even today, it's too dangerous to build on top of\nthe fault line.\n
1	en	193	0xc1d60	49622	7					10	The city center is still in ruins.\n
1	en	193	0xc1d60	49622	8					10	And to make things worse, Somoza stole the\nrecovery money.\n
1	en	193	0xc1d60	49622	9					10	We must not fail. We owe it to those who lost their\nlives.\n
