1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	0				v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	I noticed you call Che Guevara "El Che."\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	1				v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	Not just us. Everyone in these parts does.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	2				v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	"Che" was always his nickname. It does not feel\nright to call him by his last name.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	3				v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	...I was shocked the first time I saw you. You look\nso much like him.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	4				v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	I look like "El Che", huh?\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	5				v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	Sort of. Not in the face. It's more... the way you\ncarry yourself...\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	6	7397	8136	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	I guess Che's a hero to the Sandinistas, too?\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	7	8164	10156	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	Of course. The FSLN was formed in the spirit of\nthe ideologies championed by El Che and Fidel.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	8	10421	12775	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	Fidel... Fidel Castro. So you're trying to bring the\nCuban Revolution to Nicaragua.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	9	12845	14642	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	Well, we were. But Cuba isn't what it once was...\nNot since El Che left.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	10	14740	16314	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	El Che was a true revolutionary. He fought - and\ndied - for the people.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	11	16370	17387	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	He worked harder than anybody, and he was a\nrighteous man.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	12	17442	19045	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	Even as a minister of Cuba, he gave up his\nweekends to work on the farms and public works.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	13	19100	19560	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	As a volunteer, no less.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	14	19644	20271	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	Yeah, I've heard the stories.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	15	20326	21441	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	But when you think about it, wasn't it that\nobsession that did him in?\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	16	21483	21831	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	How do you mean?\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	17	21887	23517	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	We can't all be supermen. He thought the ideals he\napplied in Cuba would work in Bolivia.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	18	23558	25077	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	But, he failed to win converts and the support of\nthe peasants, and it cost him his life.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	19	25175	25927	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	Maybe... maybe you're right.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	20	26010	27278	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	But at least he did not steal from those peasants,\nno matter how hard things got.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	21	27320	27473	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	Yeah.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	22	27515	28017	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	I can sympathize with that.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	23	28100	29312	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	There's plenty of guerrillas out there who'd rob\ntheir own people to feed their revolutions.\n
1	en	196	0xc4280	50216	24	29354	31249	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0090_000_0	25	If we had a comandante like him, the Sandinistas\nwould find the will to fight.\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	0	501	1407	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	You called that giant chopper an "hombre nuevo"...\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	1	1407	2201	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	Si. It means "new man."\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	2	2229	2563	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	"New man"?\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	3	2605	3789	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	There was nobody piloting that thing. It must be\ncontrolled by machine.\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	4	3817	5391	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	Yeah, it seems that way. No human being could pull\noff those crazy maneuvers.\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	5	5433	6561	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	But it's not crazy - it's smart. It sings, too.\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	6	6603	8038	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	When we first saw it, one of my men said, "Pilot\nmust be an hombre nuevo."\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	7	8080	8721	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	Me, I do not like the name.\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	8	8735	8986	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	Why?\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	9	9000	10017	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	"Hombre nuevo" was what El Che was striving to\nbecome.\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	10	10058	57662	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	What all of us who joined the Sandinistas strive to\nbecome. That's why!\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	11				v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	An hombre nuevo is one who finds joy in virtue\nand voluntary labor...\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	12				v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	It makes me furious to see the name given to such\na monster.\n
1	en	196	0xc4bb0	50363	13				v_bri_amd0110_000_1	14	I'll bet.\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	0	459	1198	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	Chico called that helicopter el colibri...\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	1	1253	2229	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	Our name for the hummingbird. You saw how that\nchopper moved...\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	2	2270	2856	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	how it hovered in midair like a hummingbird.\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	3	2911	3650	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	Hell've a lot bigger than a bird, though.\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	4	3691	4500	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	True. But better than hombre nuevo, don't you\nthink?\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	5	4555	5419	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	When you get kidnapped by el colibri, it's all over.\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	6	5503	6673	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	They take you to a prison camp, and torture you\nuntil you snitch on your compas.\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	7	6715	7202	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	That's what took Chico...\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	8	7244	8484	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	They have no mercy. Once you've talked, they toss\nyou out like trash...\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	9	8582	9459	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	I knew this, and still I could not save Chico.\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	10	9613	10616	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	If he cannot be saved, I'll do what must be done...\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	11	10671	11187	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	Don't write him off like that.\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	12	11270	12538	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	Sometimes you have to survive, even if it means\nsacrificing your honor.\n
1	en	197	0xc5060	50438	13	12594	13486	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0120_000_1	14	I'll get him back. I promise.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	0				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	Snake, I need your opinion. How strong are the\nenemy's mercenaries?\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	1				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	They're well trained. They've got more than enough\nmen...\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	2				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	Seasoned, too - a lot of them probably saw action\nin Vietnam. They're a tough bunch.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	3				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	And armed to the teeth.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	4				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	I don't think I've ever seen a mercenary force field\nthat many tanks and attack choppers.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	5				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	It shows how much cash they have to throw\naround.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	6				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	And connections - how did they get access to\nsuch weapons?\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	7				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	How do you think? They're backed by the one and\nonly CIA.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	8				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	And here we are, half of us farmers and the other\nhalf students. Children, even!\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	9				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	And weapons... We're so short on guns we have to\nsteal them from the enemy.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	10				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	As much as I hate to say it, we're always going to\nbe on the defensive.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	11				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	I know.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	12				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	And mi viejo... Without him, we...\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	13				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	Yeah, I know.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	14				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	...I don't know if we can win.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	15				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	Can we, Snake?\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	16				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	Stop feeling sorry for yourself.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	17				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	But...\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	18				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	Amanda!\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	19				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	What?\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	20				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	Listen to me. Don't ever let your men hear you talk\nlike that.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	21				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	...I...\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	22				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	You're their leader, and a leader has to stand tall.\nEven when times get tough.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	23				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	When it feels like the fear and uncertainty could\ncrush you.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	24				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	You're the one your comrades look to for\nreassurance. That's what a leader is. Don't forget it.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	25				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	...Snake...\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	26				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	If you're looking for comfort, go find a church.\nThat's all I've got to say.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	27				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	You are right. I am sorry. I need to pull myself\ntogether.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	28				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	You'll be fine. I know you have it in you.\n
1	en	197	0xc5540	50516	29				v_bri_amd0100_000_0	30	Thank you, Snake.\n
1	en	197	0xc5eb0	50667	0					4	Claymores are directional anti-personnel landmines.\n
1	en	197	0xc5eb0	50667	1					4	Their blast radius is approximately 70 vara (60 yd),\n
1	en	197	0xc5eb0	50667	2					4	sending over 700 metal fragments through the air\nat a 60º angle.\n
1	en	197	0xc5eb0	50667	3					4	But since they're directional, you can simply disarm\nthem from their blind side.\n
