1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	0				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	The land in our country belongs to us, and yet it\ndoesn't belong to us.\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	1				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	How so?\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	2				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	Along the coast, it is all banana groves. And in the\nmountains, it is coffee.\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	3				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	I guess in that way it's not so different from here.\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	4				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	Plantations...\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	5				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	Almost all the bananas and coffee are sold as\nexports.\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	6				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	The landlords keep the money for themselves,\nleaving precious little to the farmers.\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	7				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	Worse, the biggest landowners in the country are\nSomoza and his family.\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	8				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	But it does bring in foreign currency...\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	9				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	I doubt even that, at least for bananas. The\nplantations are owned by American corporations.\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	10				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	The bananas are processed in factories on the\nplantations and exported to America from private\nports...\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	11				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	It's like having little American enclaves along the\ncoast of Nicaragua.\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	12				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	But the farmers have no choice but to go work\nthere...\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	13				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	Es ridículo! The people have to take their land\nback.\n
1	en	198	0xc62d0	50733	14				v_bri_amd0130_000_0	15	It is one of the things we're fighting for.\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	0				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	Tell me... when exactly did you realize your dad\nwas working with the KGB?\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	1				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	About six months ago. Up until then, we only had\nbeans to eat.\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	2				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	And then suddenly we started to get eggs and\nflour. Our bullet shortage simply disappeared.\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	3				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	How'd he get the cocaine?\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	4				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	Ask the KGB. All we did here was process it.\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	5				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	Coca plants grow here, too,\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	6				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	but to my knowledge almost all of the stuff we\nused came from Colombia and Bolivia.\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	7				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	It's processed in a factory and then shipped to\nports on the Caribbean Sea.\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	8				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	Where does it go after that?\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	9				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	I never thought about it.... I mean, I did not want to\nthink about it.\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	10				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	The biggest cocaine consumer in the world is the\nUnited States.\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	11				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	I'm guessing they smuggle it in on vessels\ndisguised as fishing boats.\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	12				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	Wait. La CIA uses that route, too.\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	13				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	Are you telling me they're selling cocaine to their\nown country?\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	14				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	Looks that way.\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	15				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	Those bastards are turning their own children into\njunkies? Are they insane?!\n
1	en	198	0xc6890	50825	16				v_bri_amd0140_000_0	17	No, just afraid. Afraid of a communist Central\nAmerica.\n
1	en	198	0xc6ed0	50925	0					4	La CIA calls their new toy Peace Walker, eh?\n
1	en	198	0xc6ed0	50925	1					4	Yeah... So?\n
1	en	198	0xc6ed0	50925	2					4	It is a insult to us Nicos.\n
1	en	198	0xc6ed0	50925	3					4	Because of the guy you were talking about?\nWalker?\n
