1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	0				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	Amanda! When did you join up with the Sandinistas?\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	1				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	About a year ago, when I went into the mountains\nwith mi viejo and his group.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	2				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	I thought your dad was with the FSLN from the\nstart.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	3	3719	5419	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	No. He fought alongside General Sandino, but after\nthat he retired for a while.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	4	5489	6617	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	He found a job, got a wife and a house, and raised\nus kids.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	5	6715	7453	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	Then one day some Sandinista students came by...\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	6	7481	8345	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	And he felt the old fire in his belly?\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	7	8373	9654	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	Something like that. All he did was help them\nescape from la Guardia, though.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	8	9710	10295	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	But then la Guardia showed up.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	9	10407	11549	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	They broke into our house and began pushing him\naround, shouting questions.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	10	11591	12301	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	I'm guessing he kept his mouth shut.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	11	12343	13681	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	No matter how hard they hit him. Our house was\ntrashed.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	12	13778	14935	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	After that, he was on their list - they harassed him\nday and night.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	13	15032	15966	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	It was only then that he gave himself over to the\nSandinistas.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	14	16063	17010	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	He kept it hidden from us at first, so we would not\nget hurt.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	15	17387	17916	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	He sounds like a good father.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	16	18000	19964	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	He was... But my mother got fed up with it. She left\nus. I don't blame her.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	17				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	Why didn't you go with her?\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	18				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	It was a hard decision, for sure.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	19				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	But like my father, I couldn't let Somoza get away\nwith his crimes. But most of all...\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	20				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	Chico.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	21				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	...He is too much like his papá. One way or the\nother he was going to stay.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	22				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	And I could not leave him behind.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	23				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	Soon enough la Guardia drove us out, and we\nfound ourselves in the mountains...\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	24				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	It just kind of happened\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	25				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	For an accidental revolutionary, you sure put up a\nhell of a fight.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	26				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	The mountains make men into warriors. The\ntraining is harsh,\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	27				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	but it brings us that much closer to being hombres\nnuevos.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	28				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	Chico couldn't ask for a better sister.\n
1	en	199	0xc76f0	51055	29				v_bri_amd0160_000_0	30	I can see why they picked you to be comandante.\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	0				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	When I was little, I came down with malaria.\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	1				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	Unlucky for me, it was the bad kind. I was in a\ndaze the whole time,\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	2				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	and at one point they said I was not going to make\nit.\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	3				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	Malarial encephalopathy. I hear it's pretty common\nin tropical malaria cases.\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	4				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	Even today, my memory sometimes gets a little\nfuzzy.\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	5				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	Since then I've had this fear of mosquitoes... When\nI hear them buzzing nearby, I get jumpy.\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	6				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	That explains the chain-smoking?\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	7				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	Si. I thought it might help keep the mosquitoes\naway, just a little.\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	8				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	Maybe it's all in my head. You're the same way,\nright?\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	9				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	I will say this - I prefer a cigar over mosquitoes.\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	10				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	Me, too.\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	11				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	I've gotta hand it to you. It takes guts to conquer\nyour fear like that\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	12				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	and live a guerrilla's life in the wild.\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	13				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	It is nothing. El Che did not let asthma stop him\nfrom leading the revolution.\n
1	en	200	0xc8150	51221	14				v_bri_amd0170_000_0	15	Compared to him, I am no hero.\n
1	en	200	0xc86c0	51308	0				v_bri_amd0180_000_0	12	I'm sorry to hear about your dad.\n
1	en	200	0xc86c0	51308	1				v_bri_amd0180_000_0	12	Thank you for saying that... Mi viejo was the leader\nof the frente.\n
1	en	200	0xc86c0	51308	2				v_bri_amd0180_000_0	12	He was the last of the generation that knew\nGeneral Sandino...\n
1	en	200	0xc86c0	51308	3				v_bri_amd0180_000_0	12	He saw the General's exploits first-hand as a boy.\n
1	en	200	0xc86c0	51308	4				v_bri_amd0180_000_0	12	He would tell us stories about it all the time... and\nabout how the General was assassinated.\n
1	en	200	0xc86c0	51308	5				v_bri_amd0180_000_0	12	Did you know he was getting money from the KGB?\n
1	en	200	0xc86c0	51308	6				v_bri_amd0180_000_0	12	I had some idea... But I did not have the courage to\nconfront him about it.\n
1	en	200	0xc86c0	51308	7				v_bri_amd0180_000_0	12	I know it was a painful decision for him to make.\n
1	en	200	0xc86c0	51308	8				v_bri_amd0180_000_0	12	I can imagine.\n
1	en	200	0xc86c0	51308	9				v_bri_amd0180_000_0	12	Yes, my father was a good man. I loved him as a\ndaughter. And his soldiers believed in him.\n
1	en	200	0xc86c0	51308	10				v_bri_amd0180_000_0	12	Thanks to him, la Frente held together even in the\nworst of times.\n
1	en	200	0xc86c0	51308	11				v_bri_amd0180_000_0	12	I don't know if I can ever fill his shoes...\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	0				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	Chico's 12, right?\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	1				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	Right.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	2				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	Isn't he a little... short for his age?\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	3				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	...Malnourishment. Food is hard to come by when\nyou're running around in the jungle...\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	4				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	He's got quite an appetite.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	5				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	I know!\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	6				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	I didn't want him to come in the first place.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	7				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	But there was no one to take him in. I had no\nchoice but to look after him.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	8				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	Don't be so hard on yourself.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	9				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	Sometimes it's better for a kid to be with his family\nthan far away, in a safe place.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	10				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	Thank you...\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	11				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	Promise me this, though. When your fight is over,\nmake sure he gets a proper education.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	12				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	Give him a chance to be something other than a\nguerrilla.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	13				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	It's not too late to teach him something other than\nfighting.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	14				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	OK. I promise.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	15				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	...You know what book Chico really likes?\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	16				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	The "World Encyclopedia of Mysterious Creatures."\nThe Loch Ness Monster, the Yeti...\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	17				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	UMAs. Yeah, I know.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	18				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	He's still so much like a boy... I worry about him.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	19				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	He'll be fine. I know plenty of grown men who still\ngo crazy over UMAs.\n
1	en	200	0xc8b50	51381	20				v_bri_amd0190_000_0	21	Are... are you serious?\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	0				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	You've taken such good care of me since you\nsaved me from el colibri.\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	1				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	I want to return the favor.\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	2				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	Just wait until you're healed up. Then we'll talk.\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	3				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	I appreciate that. But you need all the help you\ncan get.\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	4				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	It might take a while for me to heal completely,\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	5				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	but I'll be fine once I'm on my feet. Put me in a\ncombat unit - I'll pull my weight.\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	6				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	I wouldn't expect any less from a Sandinista\ncomandante.\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	7				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	Enough flattery.\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	8				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	But seriously, it does not feel right for me to be\nsitting here while my compas are out risking their\nlives.\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	9				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	One thing's for sure. Having you out in the field\nwould be a big boost to Sandinista morale.\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	10				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	Of course, our ultimate goal is still the overthrow\nof Somoza.\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	11				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	But until we get ourselves back in order, we will\nfollow your lead, wherever it takes us.\n
1	en	201	0xc91f0	51487	12				v_bri_amd0200_000_0	13	Glad to have you on board.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	0				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	Amanda, you getting used to Mother Base?\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	1				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	Yes, it is Heaven compared to living in the\nmountains.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	2				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	We're no longer constantly on the run from la\nGuardia or mercenaries.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	3				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	Some of the new guys we've recruited used to be\nmercenaries...\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	4				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	We're getting along. It was difficult at first,\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	5				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	but once you talk to them you realize we've got\nplenty in common.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	6				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	I see. Good to hear.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	7				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	We may be enemies, but we're all still human\nbeings...\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	8				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	La CIA's soldiers, la Guardia... The same goes for\nthe people of America.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	9				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	What's gotten into you?\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	10				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	Mi viejo got involved with drugs in order to scrape\ntogether money for la revolución.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	11				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	He did whatever the KGB said.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	12				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	All for Nicaragua... or so he told himself.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	13				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	But I realize now... In the end all he did was help\npoison young people of America.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	14				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	Yeah.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	15				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	...I've made up my mind. Even when I leave Mother\nBase and return to la revolución,\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	16				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	I will never turn to drugs. Nor will I look to the KGB\nfor help.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	17				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	If we topple Somoza using the KGB and drug\nmoney, we will lose the people's hearts.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	18				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	So you're choosing a different path from your\nfather.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	19				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	I still respect him. But I will not do things the way\nhe did.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	20				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	Well, I'm sure Chico will be glad to hear that.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	21				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	Chico is a grown soldier now. I could not face him\notherwise.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	22				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	Well said, Amanda. Those are the words of a true\ncomandante.\n
1	en	201	0xc9700	51568	23				v_bri_mis_amd0290_000_0	24	Stop... I was inspired by the greatest comandante I\nhave ever known, Boss.\n
1	en	202	0xca000	51712	0				v_bri_mis_amd0020_000_0	8	Amanda, how do I get to the prison camp?\n
1	en	202	0xca000	51712	1				v_bri_mis_amd0020_000_0	8	First head up the narrow mountain path.\n
1	en	202	0xca000	51712	2				v_bri_mis_amd0020_000_0	8	The path will gradually open up, and you'll come to\na fork in the road.\n
1	en	202	0xca000	51712	3				v_bri_mis_amd0020_000_0	8	Watch yourself up there.\n
1	en	202	0xca000	51712	4				v_bri_mis_amd0020_000_0	8	You'll be lower than the surrounding terrain,\n
1	en	202	0xca000	51712	5				v_bri_mis_amd0020_000_0	8	so if you head down the middle you'll make for an\neasy target.\n
1	en	202	0xca000	51712	6				v_bri_mis_amd0020_000_0	8	Thanks for the heads-up.\n
1	en	202	0xca000	51712	7				v_bri_mis_amd0020_000_0	8	Take the leftward path to reach the prison camp.\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	0	431	1030	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	What can you tell me about the prison camp?\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	1	1058	2117	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	Well, it used to be a village - until they took control\nof it.\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	2	2145	3065	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	It is a maze of paths, so watch out for soldiers on\npatrol.\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	3	3301	3956	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	I'll be sure not to stop and say "hi."\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	4	3984	4931	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	Use the paths carefully and you should be able to\nstay out of view.\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	5	4959	5489	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	Where are they holding Chico?\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	6	5530	6645	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	One of the houses, most likely. You can peek\nthrough the doors.\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	7	6659	7523	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	Just press <I=ACT> when the Icon appears.\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	8	7718	8735	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	You could also listen to any sounds inside for clues.\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	9	8749	9013	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	Good idea.\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	10	9041	10198	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	Guards will still be on the move while you're looking\ninside. Make sure you don't get caught.\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	11	10212	10407	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	And Snake...\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	12	10421	11187	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	I know. I'll bring him back.\n
1	en	202	0xca2d0	51757	13	11201	12051	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0	14	Thank you. I know I can count on you.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	0				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Amanda, do you know the way to the rail terminal?\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	1				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Remember the locomotive? By the fork in the road\nbefore the village?\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	2				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Yeah, back in the jungle.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	3				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Follow the train tracks from there and you'll come\nto the terminal.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	4				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	But there's a plant along the way.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	5				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Disguised as a coffee factory?\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	6				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	...Yes, it is their drug refining plant. La CIA controls\nit now.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	7				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Cutting through there is the shortest way, but it'll\nbe crawling with soldiers.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	8				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	If you want go around...\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	9				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	No, forget it. If that's the shortest way, that's the\nway I'll take.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	10				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Besides, it's one of their bases. It'll be good intel.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	11				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Very good. A number of the guards at the plant\nare positioned on high walkways.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	12				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Be sure to study their movements before you\nadvance.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	13				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Or I could just snipe them first...\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	14				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	The plant's layout is another maze, I'm afraid. Stay\ncool.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	15				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Make your way out of the plant and you'll arrive at\nthe terminal.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	16				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	You know a lot about this place...\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	17				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	What are you saying? I've been there before -\nwhen the KGB ran it - yes,\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	18				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	but it is not as if I enjoyed it.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	19				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	No, I just meant you know a lot about how the\nenemy works.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	20				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	I hope so.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	21				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Anyway, did you talk to Chico about the terminal?\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	22				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	He said it's where they transfer the cargo onto\ntrucks.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	23				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Meaning the facility is of considerable importance\nto them. Don't get careless.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	24				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	I won't.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	25				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	By the way,\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	26				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	I've heard of a shortcut that cuts straight to the\ncoffee factory to the east of the village,\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	27				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	but I've never used it myself. Check it out if you're\ninterested.\n
1	en	202	0xca770	51831	28				v_bri_mis_amd0030_000_0	29	Thanks for the tip.\n
1	en	203	0xcb100	51984	0	445	1226	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0	9	An enemy tank! Is there somewhere you can hide,\nBoss?\n
1	en	203	0xcb100	51984	1	1253	2215	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0	9	There are train cars, but they won't hold up\nagainst a gun like that.\n
1	en	203	0xcb100	51984	2	2243	2869	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0	9	Even a freight train? Incredible!\n
1	en	203	0xcb100	51984	3	3009	3887	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0	9	But they'd keep me out of sight - temporarily.\n
1	en	203	0xcb100	51984	4	3914	5196	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0	9	Use them to look for an opportunity to hit its\ntreads or the fuel tank at the back, but...\n
1	en	203	0xcb100	51984	5	5196	5781	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0	9	Don't forget about that gun, huh?\n
1	en	203	0xcb100	51984	6	5795	6506	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0	9	Or the soldiers. They may try to flank you.\n
1	en	203	0xcb100	51984	7	6520	6645	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0	9	Right.\n
1	en	203	0xcb100	51984	8	6645	8219	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0	9	You can also stop it by taking out all the soldiers.\nYou can do it, Snake!\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	0	445	1657	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	Amanda, do I have to take the fork in the road\nback to the village?\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	1	1685	2925	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	People say there is a shortcut. Go back to the\ncoffee factory entrance,\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	2	2939	3469	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	then follow the path on the right.\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	3	3496	4082	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	That will take you straight to the village.\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	4	4109	4820	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	They may have increased security in that area,\nthough.\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	5	5015	6534	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	Not surprising, after what happened with the tank.\nWhat do I do once I'm back at the village?\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	6	6561	8010	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	Destroy the barricade at the north side. From\nthere you can reconnect with the transport route.\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	7	8024	8874	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	Hmm... I'll need C4 for that.\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	8	8888	9738	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	The explosion will bring everyone running too.\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	9	9766	10727	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	There's probably going to be a fight - one way or\nthe other.\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	10	10755	11730	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	They might not see you if you stick to the\nnarrower pathways.\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	11	11800	12552	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	Then just climb over any obstacles.\n
1	en	203	0xcb450	52037	12	12566	13583	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0	13	Don't let your guard down after taking out the\nbarricade, either.\n
1	en	203	0xcb950	52117	0	445	1226	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0	11	Chico says there's a bridge north of the village.\n
1	en	203	0xcb950	52117	1	1253	2020	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0	11	Yes, a narrow one - for crossing the pipe.\n
1	en	203	0xcb950	52117	2	2159	2981	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0	11	On the other side of that is the road the trucks\nuse,\n
1	en	203	0xcb950	52117	3	3023	3482	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0	11	though it's collapsed in places.\n
1	en	203	0xcb950	52117	4	3622	4249	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0	11	I'll have nowhere to run if they spot me.\n
1	en	203	0xcb950	52117	5	4263	4792	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0	11	They could be blocking the road, too.\n
1	en	203	0xcb950	52117	6	4820	5182	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0	11	Is there another way?\n
1	en	203	0xcb950	52117	7	5196	5851	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0	11	There is a path along the cliff.\n
1	en	203	0xcb950	52117	8	5879	6993	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0	11	After you cross the bridge, there are ruins of a\nfort on the mountain.\n
1	en	203	0xcb950	52117	9	7049	7704	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0	11	Going through there would be a little easier.\n
1	en	203	0xcb950	52117	10	7746	8888	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0	11	Once you come to the end of the mountain path,\nyou'll be at the fort.\n
1	en	203	0xcbd00	52176	0	431	1950	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0	9	That fort was built during the civil war. It seems la\nCIA's troops are occupying it, now.\n
1	en	203	0xcbd00	52176	1	2187	2856	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0	9	This just gets better and better.\n
1	en	203	0xcbd00	52176	2	2883	3859	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0	9	They've got gun turrets set up all around, from the\nlooks of it.\n
1	en	203	0xcbd00	52176	3	3887	4959	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0	9	Attract too much attention and you'll really stir up\nthe hornet's nest.\n
1	en	203	0xcbd00	52176	4	4973	5558	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0	9	Maybe I'll try and find a way around.\n
1	en	203	0xcbd00	52176	5	5600	6854	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0	9	You could always commandeer one of the turrets -\na little target practice, perhaps?\n
1	en	203	0xcbd00	52176	6				v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0	9	Just like Krasnogorje.\n
1	en	203	0xcbd00	52176	7				v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0	9	Krasno-what?\n
1	en	203	0xcbd00	52176	8				v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0	9	Sorry, just... thinking about old times.\n
1	en	204	0xcc050	52229	0				v_bri_mis_amd0070_000_0	8	Watch out! It's el galápago!\n
1	en	204	0xcc050	52229	1				v_bri_mis_amd0070_000_0	8	It reduces its body weight by blasting air\nunderneath it.\n
1	en	204	0xcc050	52229	2				v_bri_mis_amd0070_000_0	8	That makes it a lot faster than any tank. It also\nhas a tight turning radius.\n
1	en	204	0xcc050	52229	3				v_bri_mis_amd0070_000_0	8	Any weak points?\n
1	en	204	0xcc050	52229	4				v_bri_mis_amd0070_000_0	8	Taking out its boosters could reduce its\nacceleration...\n
1	en	204	0xcc050	52229	5				v_bri_mis_amd0070_000_0	8	You could also try destroying its machine guns.\n
1	en	204	0xcc050	52229	6				v_bri_mis_amd0070_000_0	8	I'll give it a shot.\n
1	en	204	0xcc050	52229	7				v_bri_mis_amd0070_000_0	8	We've lost many compas to that thing. Send it to\nthe scrapyard!\n
1	en	204	0xcc320	52274	0	459	1894	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0	11	From here on in you'll be in a cloud forest. The\nground is covered in vegetation.\n
1	en	204	0xcc320	52274	1	1922	2897	0x0e3bb338	v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0	11	You'll have plenty of hiding places, but so will the\nenemy.\n
