1	en	222	0xde520	56914	0				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	So what's an 'expert system?'\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	1				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	The AI housed within Peace Walker began\ndevelopment as such a system.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	2				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	An expert system is a type of proxy program\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	3				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	by which a computer makes decisions as an expert\nwould.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	4				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	The program "MYCIN," for example,\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	5				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	is a system that decides which kinds of antibiotics\nto prescribe.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	6				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	The system asks the patient a series of questions\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	7				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	to narrow down the range of appropriate drugs.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	8				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	So you programmed Peace Walker to prescribe live\nnuclear warheads instead of penicillin.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	9				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	What I realized, however, was that a simple expert\nsystem wasn't up to the task.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	10				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	You need more than expertise to launch a nuke.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	11				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	Indeed. Expertise is a necessary prerequisite but\ninsufficient on its own.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	12				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	Deciding to launch a retaliatory strike requires\nconsideration of a wider range of factors.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	13				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	In such a scenario, the entire global situation\nbecomes the criterion for making a decision.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	14				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	Makes sense. You screw up the prescription, and\nthe whole world goes into anaphylactic shock.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	15				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	A "weak AI"\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	16				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	that has only a limited range of knowledge upon\nwhich to base its decisions won't cut it.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	17				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	Therefore, I had the AI study The Boss' thought\npatterns,\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	18				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	thus creating a true expert system - a "strong AI."\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	19				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	You couldn't leave the world in the hands of\nsomething\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	20				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	with anything less than an absolute worldview.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	21				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	I could have built a simple expert system in no\ntime at all.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	22				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	Say, how would you like a system that decides\nwhich guns you should equip\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	23				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	according to the mission's parameters?\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	24				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	I'll pass. I'm not gonna leave my life up to\nsomebody else's judgment.\n
1	en	222	0xde520	56914	25				v_bri_dsl0050_000_1	26	Especially not a machine.\n
1	en	222	0xdeeb0	57067	0					3	With current technology, AI are inevitably enormous\nin size.\n
1	en	222	0xdeeb0	57067	1					3	But as circuit integration continues to advance,\nthey'll become even smaller.\n
1	en	222	0xdeeb0	57067	2					3	As small as human brains, and perhaps smaller\nthan that.\n
