1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	0	571	1267	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	What did you mean by "the Ghost in the Machine"?\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	1	1281	2633	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	Oh, that... It's a term coined by the philosopher\nGilbert Ryle.\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	2	2661	3232	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	You've heard of Descartes, yes?\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	3	3260	3817	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	"I think, therefore I am..."\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	4	3845	5419	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	That is the one. Descartes espoused the dualistic\ntheory of mind and body.\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	5	5433	6715	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	He believed that our thinking minds exist in a\nseparate dimension from our bodies,\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	6	6743	7397	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	which are governed by the laws of physics.\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	7	7467	9041	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	But if that were true, then couldn't you say that a\nmechanical "body"\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	8	9125	10337	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	inhabited by a ghost "mind" is a human being?\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	9	10407	11340	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	Ryle criticized Descartes on those grounds,\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	10	11340	12469	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	saying such a thing surely wouldn't be human.\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	11	12469	12817	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	Why'd you bring it up?\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	12	12845	13848	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	I wasn't thinking of Ryle in particular when I said it.\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	13	13904	15450	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	I simply thought that if a person is composed of a\nmachine and a ghost,\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	14	15575	16272	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	perhaps the opposite is true as well.\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	15	16342	18752	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	Perhaps by placing a ghost inside a machine, we\ncould in effect give birth to a new person.\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	16	18780	19462	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	And that was your idea for the Boss AI?\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	17	19490	20953	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	The moment you ripped the memory board out, the\nMammal Pod ceased to function.\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	18	21023	21441	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	It should have been dead.\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	19	21524	23252	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	And yet Peace Walker righted itself, singing a song\nof peace.\n
1	en	224	0xe0230	57379	20	23294	25161	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0080_000_0	21	I couldn't help but feel... that her soul had come to\ninhabit Peace Walker.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	0				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	Are you familiar with the film "2001: A Space\nOdyssey"?\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	1				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	I've heard of it, but...\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	2				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	Of course not. I didn't expect you to be cultured\nenough to appreciate such things.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	3				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	Yeah, thanks. Anyway...\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	4				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	"2001" features an AI called HAL,\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	5				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	a highly advanced system that controls an\nexploration spacecraft.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	6				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	It can converse with people, and even play chess.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	7				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	Huh. Now where have I heard that before...\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	8				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	The way HAL was portrayed was truly superb.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	9				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	How so?\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	10				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	HAL is given secret orders that not even the\nship's captain knows about.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	11				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	Naturally, he's not allowed to divulge them to the\ncrew. The stress of it causes HAL to crack.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	12				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	Crack?\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	13				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	Go crazy. Though there are those who interpret it\ndifferently.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	14				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	One by one, HAL kills off the crew until the captain\nfinally shuts it down...\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	15				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	The film offers amazing insights into AI - their\ngrowth, their utility, their faults - and their fear of\ndeath.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	16				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	You must have found it useful in your research,\nthen.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	17				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	Must you always be so... utilitarian?\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	18				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	It doesn't matter whether or not it's useful. What\nmatters is that it inspired me.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	19				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	Then it was USEFUL.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	20				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	Never mind. The portrayal of HAL wasn't the only\nwonderful thing about the film.\n
1	en	224	0xe0990	57497	21				v_bri_dsl0100_000_1	22	It was full of hints about the future of human\nevolution. Truly a film for the ages.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	0				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	Strangelove, when did you and The Boss first\nmeet?\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	1				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	...Did she ever tell you about what she saw in\nspace?\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	2				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	Yeah.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	3				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	I saw the same thing along with her.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	4				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	The Soviets beat America into space with Sputnik,\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	5				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	and so America rushed to be first in manned\nspaceflight.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	6				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	NASA used her as their top-secret guinea pig,\nlaunching her deep into the cold blackness of\nspace.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	7				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	I took part in the project. As a scientist.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	8				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	You were there with her...?\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	9				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	Yes... For a brief time, we were one and the same,\nshe and I.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	10				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	We sought each other out... Completed each other.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	11				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	Did you know that inside every woman there's a\nuniverse,\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	12				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	and that we are able to sense this in each other.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	13				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	We connected because of our empathetic female\nbrains.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	14				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	As time went on... I began to have doubts about\noffering such a noble soul as sacrifice.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	15				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	Why would they...? Why did she have to...?\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	16				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	...The flight test was a narrow success, and she\nmiraculously made it back alive.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	17				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	But her mind and body were horribly mangled, and\nthere was nothing I could do for her.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	18				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	We were no longer one and the same.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	19				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	She went away, and I, having nothing else to live\nfor, immersed myself in AI research.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	20				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	Hoping that no one would ever have to make her\nsacrifice again.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	21				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	I never knew...\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	22				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	It's not really worth knowing.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	23				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	We were ships passing in the night, that's all.\n
1	en	225	0xe1160	57622	24				v_bri_dsl0110_000_1	25	Perhaps someday I'll tell you the long version, if\nyou're interested.\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	0	445	1448	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	That was quite a warm welcome you gave me at\nthe base in Costa Rica.\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	1	1476	2465	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	...Sorry about that. But I simply had to know.\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	2	2493	2953	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	The Boss' final act?\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	3	2981	4778	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	Yes. By inputting her thoughts and actions into the\nAI, I was imbuing it with her mind.\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	4	4848	5921	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	The only thing I couldn't understand was her final\nact.\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	5	5935	6450	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	Operation Snake Eater...\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	6	6478	8874	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	Official history says she betrayed her homeland\nand defected to the enemy... and was killed by you.\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	7	8944	10644	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	...But it didn't make sense. The Boss would be the\nlast person on earth to betray her country.\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	8	10699	11326	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	It was logically inconsistent.\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	9	11368	11744	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	...It was, wasn't it?\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	10	11772	13096	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	That internal inconsistency prevented the AI from\nactivating properly -\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	11	13151	13862	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	just as HAL malfunctioned in the film.\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	12	13904	14907	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	I understood the reasoning. But I had to have\nproof.\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	13	15004	16495	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	Proof of her final act. Her true intentions. One way\nor another!\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	14	16509	17233	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	So you tried to squeeze it out of me, huh?\n
1	en	225	0xe1a10	57761	15	17247	19560	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0120_000_1	16	As a matter of fact, I did. Your silence was the\nvery answer I was looking for.\n
1	en	226	0xe2720	57970	0	459	1156	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0140_000_1	13	What did you think of Peace Walker's final act?\n
1	en	226	0xe2720	57970	1	1170	2089	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0140_000_1	13	I recreated her thought patterns exactly.\n
1	en	226	0xe2720	57970	2	2159	2800	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0140_000_1	13	It was exactly what she would have done.\n
1	en	226	0xe2720	57970	3	2883	4249	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0140_000_1	13	The world's most empathetic mind weighed the\npast, the future,\n
