1	en	226	0xe2720	57970	5	5670	6339	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0140_000_1	13	Merely knowing that is enough for me.\n
1	en	226	0xe2720	57970	6	6436	7801	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0140_000_1	13	...So what you're saying is, we don't need\ndeterrence to have peace?\n
1	en	226	0xe2720	57970	7	7815	9278	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0140_000_1	13	I didn't say that. What's important is that we wish\nfor peace.\n
1	en	226	0xe2720	57970	8	9320	10532	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0140_000_1	13	MSF needs a way to protect itself from the might\nof nations.\n
1	en	226	0xe2720	57970	9	10588	11661	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0140_000_1	13	Survival requires pragmatic thought and action.\n
1	en	226	0xe2720	57970	10	11758	12552	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0140_000_1	13	But, you still must retain your ideals.\n
1	en	226	0xe2720	57970	11	12705	14224	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0140_000_1	13	If the gap between reality and those ideals ever\nleads you to lose them...\n
1	en	226	0xe2720	57970	12	14363	15088	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0140_000_1	13	I doubt MSF will survive.\n
1	en	226	0xe2bb0	58043	0					16	Strangelove... Is that a code name?\n
1	en	226	0xe2bb0	58043	1					16	No, just a nickname.\n
1	en	226	0xe2bb0	58043	2					16	Don't tell me you don't recognize it! From Kubrick's\n"Dr. Strangelove, or How I Learned to Stop\nWorrying and Love the Bomb?"\n
1	en	226	0xe2bb0	58043	3					16	It's a film that came out in 1964... a dark comedy\nabout the absurdity of nuclear deterrence.\n
