1	en	227	0xe3280	58152	3	3441	4388	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0160_000_1	20	I started out at NASA. That's where I met her.\n
1	en	227	0xe3280	58152	4	4416	4890	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0160_000_1	20	When Boss went into space...\n
1	en	227	0xe3280	58152	5	4917	6339	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0160_000_1	20	...Yes. It was that incident that turned me away\nfrom aerospace engineering.\n
1	en	227	0xe3280	58152	6	6422	7397	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0160_000_1	20	Space is entirely too hazardous a place for human\nbeings.\n
1	en	227	0xe3280	58152	7	7467	8373	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0160_000_1	20	That was why I felt an immediate need to develop\nAI.\n
1	en	227	0xe3280	58152	8	8442	10267	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0160_000_1	20	As it turned out, rockets later became much safer,\nand mankind reached the surface of the moon...\n
1	en	227	0xe3280	58152	9	10351	11466	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0160_000_1	20	In any event, it was a hollow Cold War victory.\n
1	en	227	0xe3280	58152	10	11563	13096	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0160_000_1	20	When you get down to it, a nuclear missile is just a\nrocket with a nuclear warhead strapped to it.\n
1	en	227	0xe3280	58152	11	13165	14698	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0160_000_1	20	Thus, taking the initiative in the space race was\ntantamount to a military show of force.\n
1	en	227	0xe3280	58152	12	14795	16021	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0160_000_1	20	But the budgetary strain was too big for\nWashington or Moscow to handle.\n
