1	en	228	0xe4f40	58612	19					1	h��\n�VW\n����ڞW��A`�B��u��'B�%�:Ό�X_���?ee9����fL�;��#3P�4шh�M�F�V������bܺ�U����Fw�ڔ�a�IBE��Q�%p+�ی�w�8�i��S�%����Yx׷0c�ʧ ���o{��O\t"�_����-#ڮ1�gy� 
1	en	229	0xe5620	58722	0	487	1407	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0	11	Huey's probably mentioned this, but just to be clear,\n
1	en	229	0xe5620	58722	1	1448	2507	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0	11	there's a limit to the parts we can produce here at\nMother Base.\n
1	en	229	0xe5620	58722	2	2549	4123	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0	11	Therefore, I've built ZEKE's AI using memory boards\nyou pulled from other AI weapons.\n
1	en	229	0xe5620	58722	3	4123	4388	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0	11	Will that work?\n
1	en	229	0xe5620	58722	4	4402	5726	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0	11	In the human brain, individual functions are spread\nacross multiple regions.\n
1	en	229	0xe5620	58722	5	5767	7746	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0	11	The same is true of AI. Multiple parts sharing the\nsame function interlink to strengthen that function.\n
1	en	229	0xe5620	58722	6	7760	8874	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0	11	For example, the more sensor memory boards you\nhave,\n
1	en	229	0xe5620	58722	7	8888	9975	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0	11	the greater ZEKE's search-and-detect capabilities\nwill be.\n
1	en	229	0xe5620	58722	8	10031	11215	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0	11	Install more movement boards and you'll increase\nits mobility.\n
1	en	229	0xe5620	58722	9	11215	12496	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0	11	Meaning the AI's capabilities change depending on\nhow much memory we give it?\n
1	en	229	0xe5620	58722	10	12510	14113	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0	11	Exactly. The more boards you install, the more\npowerful a function will be.\n
1	en	229	0xe5ac0	58796	0	459	1239	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0090_000_0	9	How's the ZEKE AI different from Peace Walker's?\n
1	en	229	0xe5ac0	58796	1	1239	2452	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0090_000_0	9	ZEKE's AI isn't a replica of the human thought\nprocess.\n
1	en	229	0xe5ac0	58796	2	2452	3622	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0090_000_0	9	It isn't programmed to make decisions about\nnuclear retaliation.\n
1	en	229	0xe5ac0	58796	3	3775	5126	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0090_000_0	9	On the other hand, it is capable of highly\nindependent action in combat\n
1	en	229	0xe5ac0	58796	4	5126	5879	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0090_000_0	9	when given orders from a pilot.\n
1	en	229	0xe5ac0	58796	5	5921	7718	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0090_000_0	9	It can protect infantry, destroy the enemy, and, if\nordered...\n
1	en	229	0xe5ac0	58796	6	7760	8052	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0090_000_0	9	Launch a nuke.\n
1	en	229	0xe5ac0	58796	7	8080	8902	0x0ebd8542	v_bri_dsl0090_000_0	9	Let us hope it never comes to that.\n
1	en	229	0xe5ac0	58796	8	8930	9529	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_dsl0090_000_0	9	My sentiments exactly.\n
1	en	229	0xe5dd0	58845	0					7	I'd better fill you in on ZEKE's speech synthesis\nsystem.\n
1	en	229	0xe5dd0	58845	1					7	Speech synthesis system?\n
1	en	229	0xe5dd0	58845	2					7	Humans speak for the conventional weapons they\nwield,\n
1	en	229	0xe5dd0	58845	3					7	but an autonomous AI weapon is a different story.\n
1	en	229	0xe5dd0	58845	4					7	If the AI can't communicate with surrounding\nforces, how can they function as a unit?\n
1	en	229	0xe5dd0	58845	5					7	True. Verbal communication is critical on the\nbattlefield.\n
1	en	229	0xe5dd0	58845	6					7	Thus, an AI weapon requires a dedicated system to\nproduce speech.\n
