1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	0	459	1072	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	Let's go over this one more time.\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	1	1072	2020	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	First, I need an ID card to get into the lab.\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	2	2020	3385	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	That is correct. From the outside it looks like any\nother ruin.\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	3	3427	4778	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	But on the inside it is a state-of-the-art research\nfacility.\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	4	4806	6185	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	And your ID card got taken away from you by\nsome guy in an orange jacket.\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	5	6255	7314	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	Exactly. I heard a quetzal singing nearby.\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	6	7453	8164	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	It has not been that long since it happened.\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	7	8568	10072	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	It could be tricky if he's out on patrol, but if he's a\nstationary sentry...\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	8	10114	10741	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	You don't think the quetzal's moved?\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	9	10825	12441	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	Its nest is probably nearby. I do not think it will go\naway anytime soon.\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	10	12483	13318	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	Good. I'll get on looking for that soldier.\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	11	13332	14572	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	If you forget what it sounds like, I'll do the call for\nyou again.\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	12	14642	15729	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	Just give me a call anytime you'd like to hear it.\n
1	en	231	0xe75f0	59231	13	16049	16425	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0030_000_0	14	I'll do that.\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	0	459	1866	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	Let me get this straight. You were in Costa Rica\nas a birdwatcher?\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	1	1894	3413	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	Yes, I was. Not for pleasure, though - I am a\nresearcher, after all.\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	2	3496	4639	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	I am studying the distribution of Latin American\nbird species.\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	3	4764	5614	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	With today's compact cassette tape recorders,\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	4	5656	6896	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	even a woman like me can carry her recording\nequipment by herself.\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	5	7077	7843	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	But it was a mistake to come alone.\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	6	7913	9445	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	Mmm. Even so, there sure are a lot of wild birds in\nCosta Rica.\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	7	9696	10685	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	Aren't there? Over 800 different species,\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	8	10741	11925	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	said to be more than 10% of all living bird species\non Earth.\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	9	12092	13235	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	How many can you name, Mr. Ornithologist?\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	10	13332	14349	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	Hey, I was just trying not to scare you...\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	11	14391	15325	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	You should at least have a basic knowledge of\nCosta Rica.\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	12	15394	16648	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	How about this: I will give you a thorough\neducation,\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	13	35876	13513	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	Mr. First-Time Ornithologist.\n
1	en	231	0xe7ae0	59310	14				v_bri_ccl0090_000_0	15	Uh, OK. Start by telling me about the quetzal.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	0				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Cécile, what's that machine you said you use to\nmake those recordings of yours?\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	1				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	A cassette... something or other.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	2				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	A cassette recorder? Or a cassette densuke, as\nthey say in Japon.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	3				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Yeah, that. What is that thing, anyway?\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	4				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	A portable recording device released last year by a\nJapanese company: Sony.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	5				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	It uses compact cassettes, making it far lighter\nthan open reel machines.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	6				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	It still weighs 5 kilograms, but the exercise won't\nkill me!\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	7				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Ha.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	8				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	It's user-friendly, too.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	9				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	All the buttons have markings on them,\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	10				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	allowing you to operate it without looking at it.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	11				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Can you imagine missing the shot of a lifetime\nsimply because you'd blinked?\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	12				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	That would be devastating.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	13				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	But where'd they come up with densuke? It sounds\nlike a Japanese name.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	14				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Allow me to field that one.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	15				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Kaz?!\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	16				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Densuke's a nickname that comes from the name\nof an old manga character.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	17				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Was he some recording nerd, too?\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	18				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Don't gimme that! Recording atmospheric noises is\nan exhilarating art!\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	19				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	There's nothing like capturing the real world in\naction on tape!\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	20				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	It's just like taking pictures with a camera,\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	21				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	only with a microphone instead of a viewfinder.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	22				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Sure...\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	23				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Listen to a tape with your eyes closed\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	24				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	and the scene just bursts to life in your mind's eye.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	25				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Tell him, Cécile.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	26				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Absolutely. When I listen to the sounds of birds in\nmy apartment,\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	27				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	it's like I'm back in the forest where I recorded\nthem.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	28				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	See, she's a Parisienne. She knows what's chic.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	29				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	If you say so...\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	30				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	What do you like to record, Monsieur Miller?\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	31				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Me? Steam locomotives, no question.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	32				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	The roar of the engine, the throaty steam whistle...\nMore animal than machine.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	33				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Mmh, don't get me started!\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	34				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Steam locomotives are a dying breed in Japan.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	35				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	I wouldn't mind going back for a bit and making\nsome new tapes while I still can.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	36				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	...You're less civilized than I thought.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	37				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	L-LESS civilized?!\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	38				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	I detest those beasts. The noise frightens off all\nthe birds.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	39				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Then there's the smoke...\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	40				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	I much prefer the peace and quiet of the forest.\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	41				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Cécile, wait! That... That came out wrong, I...\n
1	en	232	0xe8030	59395	42				v_bri_mis_ccl0010_000_0	43	Sure it did.\n
1	en	232	0xe8da0	59610	0					7	Alright, what do you want to know about quetzals?\n
1	en	232	0xe8da0	59610	1					7	Hmm... Give me the basics, something that'll help\nme find one.\n
1	en	232	0xe8da0	59610	2					7	OK, then. First of all, as I'm sure you remember,\n
1	en	232	0xe8da0	59610	3					7	the quetzal's wings and back are emerald green\n
1	en	232	0xe8da0	59610	4					7	- a dazzling blend of viridian fading into blue.\n
1	en	232	0xe8da0	59610	5					7	Its belly is brilliant red, and its tail feathers are\nwhite. Such a gorgeous bird...\n
1	en	232	0xe8da0	59610	6					7	Also, the male has two long decorative feathers,\nbut only during breeding season.\n
