1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	0	445	1351	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	The Scarlet Macaw and the Great Green Macaw\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	1	1351	2229	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	are also representative birds of Costa Rica.\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	2	2368	3608	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	Macaws are a type of parrot... enormous, stately\nbirds.\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	3	3761	4931	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	Macaw... I think I've heard that name somewhere\nbefore.\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	4	5168	6144	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	But of course you have - you're an ornithologist,\nno?\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	5	6171	6492	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	Stop it....\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	6	6673	8122	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	So tell me, where do macaws live in Costa Rica\ntoday?\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	7	8192	8721	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	Oh c'mon now...\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	8	9139	9696	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	I am only teasing you.\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	9	9752	10574	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	Macaws live not in the cloud forests,\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	10	10574	11772	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	but in the rain forests on the Pacific side of Costa\nRica.\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	11	11842	13207	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	In the past, they were a common sight all across\nthe country,\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	12	13249	14419	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	but lately the population has decreased\ndramatically.\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	13	14517	16384	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	One possible cause is the pesticides sprayed to\nfacilitate large-scale banana cultivation.\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	14	16467	17136	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	Evicted from their own land, huh.\n
1	en	235	0xeb310	60209	15	17164	18543	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0150_000_0	16	Thankfully, conservation efforts have been gaining\nsome momentum lately.\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	0				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	Never heard the name "Cosima" before.\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	1				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	The again I don't know many people from France.\nIs it a common name?\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	2				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	No. Not that common.\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	3				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	But Wagner's second wife was named Cosima\nFrancesca Gaetana Wagner.\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	4				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	Huh.\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	5				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	You know, "Kojima" is a common last name in Japan.\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	6				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	Kaz?!\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	7				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	It's just funny how, you know,\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	8				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	I'm part Japanese and Cécile's middle name is so\nclose to "Kojima."\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	9				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	It feels like... destiny unfolding.\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	10				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	You think so?\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	11				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	Oui oui! That's a beautiful name you have. Cécile\nCosima Caminades.\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	12				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	Wait a second...\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	13				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	Cécile Cosima Caminades... Cosima Caminades...\nHey, that’s close to...\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	14				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	Close to what?\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	15				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	Your name... It sounds almost like the sentence\n“Kojima, kaminandesu” in Japanese.\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	16				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	And what does it mean, s’il vous plait?\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	17				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	Well, "kami" is the word for "god" in Japanese.\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	18				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	"Nandesu..." Well, it's hard to explain, but placed\nafter "god" it would turn the sentence into "is God."\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	19				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	Okay. So?!\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	20				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	"Kojima is God"... Cecile's name is a message!\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	21				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	I don’t believe it... Kojima is God... Kojima is God...\n
1	en	235	0xeb860	60294	22				v_bri_ccl0151_000_0	23	Umm, Kaz...?\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	0	445	1253	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	Did you live in Paris your whole life before coming\nhere?\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	1	1434	2368	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	Yes. It is my favorite city.\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	2	2549	3566	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	Paris is the world capital of art and culture.\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	3	3664	5489	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	It has the latest fashion, the best cuisine, and the\nmost elegant, refined people.\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	4	5614	7147	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	The beauty of the Champs-Élysées at night is\nalmost unearthly.\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	5	7230	8554	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	The name comes from Elysium, the name of\nParadise in Greek mythology.\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	6	8721	9236	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	Heaven, in other words.\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	7	9654	10755	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	Must be nice for some people. Not for me.\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	8	10769	11674	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	Are you saying the cultured life does not appeal to\nyou?\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	9	11688	13151	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	I'm saying I never had a chance to lead one. Not\nthat it appealed to me anyway.\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	10	13165	13583	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	You prefer war?\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	11	13597	15464	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	I don't... Like war. Life outside heaven just suits me\nbetter.\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	12	15492	16077	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	That is a hard way to live...\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	13	16119	17902	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	...But if you do ever come to France, I will show\nyou around Paris.\n
1	en	236	0xec6f0	60527	14	18000	19253	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0040_000_0	15	Then you will see what heaven on earth is really\nlike.\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	0	459	1978	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	Heaven on earth, huh... The only image I have of\nFrance is the Foreign Legion.\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	1				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	Th-that is how you view France?!\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	2				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	What do the French think of the them?\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	3				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	It is a difficult question... We normally don't think\nabout it so much.\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	4				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	Critics claim it forces foreigners to take on the\nmost dangerous missions\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	5				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	so French citizens won't get hurt.\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	6				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	You're right, that probably had something to do\nwith why it was created...\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	7				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	But I understand that along with service comes\nbenefits\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	8				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	such as French citizenship and permanent\nresidency.\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	9				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	Those who join are all given an equal chance,\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	10				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	regardless of race, religion, education, social\nstatus, or national origin.\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	11				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	So it can be a godsend for people from poor\ncountries.\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	12				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	A way for the have-nots to live a decent life...\n
1	en	236	0xecc30	60611	13				v_bri_ccl0050_000_0	14	I guess that's not so different from MSF.\n
1	en	237	0xed150	60693	0	459	1630	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0060_000_0	13	There's one other image I have of France: the\nnational anthem.\n
1	en	237	0xed150	60693	1	1643	3260	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0060_000_0	13	Ah, La Marseillaise... Not everyone is a fan, of\ncourse.\n
1	en	237	0xed150	60693	2	3622	5057	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0060_000_0	13	The whole "To arms, citizens. May an impure blood\nwater our furrows." thing, eh?\n
1	en	237	0xed150	60693	3	5071	6283	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0060_000_0	13	The song was composed right after the French\nRevolution.\n
1	en	237	0xed150	60693	4	6352	7188	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0060_000_0	13	Fearing what the tide of the Revolution\nrepresented,\n
1	en	237	0xed150	60693	5	7202	7941	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0060_000_0	13	the ruling classes in neighboring countries applied\n
1	en	237	0xed150	60693	6	7941	8791	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0060_000_0	13	all kinds of pressure on the young government.\n
1	en	237	0xed150	60693	7	8818	10253	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0060_000_0	13	La Marseillaise became the anthem of the\nvolunteer armies that sought to protect\n
1	en	237	0xed150	60693	8	10267	11145	0x0ec8dda0	v_bri_ccl0060_000_0	13	constitutional rule against that pressure.\n
1	en	237	0xed150	60693	9	11159	11911	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_ccl0060_000_0	13	And they couldn't do that without armed force.\n
