1	en	246	0xf6670	63079	0	431	2340	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0070_000_0	9	The aim of the Peace Walker Project is to achieve\nrobust nuclear deterrence across Central America\n
1	en	246	0xf6670	63079	1	2368	3538	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0070_000_0	9	by deploying a new nuclear weapon system along\nthe Caribbean coast.\n
1	en	246	0xf6670	63079	2	3566	4430	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0070_000_0	9	Peace Walker is also the name of the system itself.\n
1	en	246	0xf6670	63079	3	4639	6213	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_huy0070_000_0	9	A nuclear weapon named "Peace"... I can just see\nthe look on Kaz's face.\n
1	en	246	0xf6670	63079	4	6241	7300	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_huy0070_000_0	9	So why exactly does this new system need legs in\nthe first place?\n
1	en	246	0xf6670	63079	5	7300	7704	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0070_000_0	9	Because it's a "Walker."\n
1	en	246	0xf6670	63079	6	7704	8094	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0070_000_0	9	An unmanned weapon\n
1	en	246	0xf6670	63079	7	8094	9613	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0070_000_0	9	moving under its own power and capable of\nlaunching a deterrent strike from anywhere...\n
1	en	246	0xf6670	63079	8	9738	10671	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0070_000_0	9	That's the whole idea behind Peace Walker.\n
1	en	246	0xf6a00	63136	0	459	1476	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_000_0	11	The reason Peace Walker is a mobile nuclear\nweapons system\n
1	en	246	0xf6a00	63136	1	1476	2452	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_000_0	11	is to maximize its potential as a nuclear deterrent.\n
1	en	246	0xf6a00	63136	2	2465	2730	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_huy0080_000_0	11	How so?\n
1	en	246	0xf6a00	63136	3	2730	3873	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_000_0	11	If need be, Peace Walker can stay constantly on\nthe move\n
1	en	246	0xf6a00	63136	4	3873	4764	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_000_0	11	so that the adversary can't pinpoint its position...\n
1	en	246	0xf6a00	63136	5	4834	5684	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_000_0	11	That allows it to avoid preemptive enemy strikes.\n
1	en	246	0xf6a00	63136	6	5684	6645	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_huy0080_000_0	11	So you're saying it keeps the retaliation card in\nplay.\n
1	en	246	0xf6a00	63136	7	6645	7397	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_000_0	11	Coldman likes to brag about it in this way...\n
1	en	246	0xf6a00	63136	8	7397	8219	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_huy0080_000_0	11	Like a land-based version of an SSBN.\n
1	en	246	0xf6a00	63136	9	8233	9013	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_000_0	11	And there's another reason for them to be mobile.\n
1	en	246	0xf6a00	63136	10	9097	10184	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_000_0	11	Peace Walker also has a self-destruct function.\n
1	en	246	0xf6dc0	63196	0					8	Why would Peace Walker need a self-destruct\nfunction?\n
1	en	246	0xf6dc0	63196	1					8	You saw it, didn't you, Snake? That sphere on\nPeace Walker's head?\n
1	en	246	0xf6dc0	63196	2					8	Yeah.\n
1	en	246	0xf6dc0	63196	3					8	That's a hydrogen bomb.\n
1	en	246	0xf6dc0	63196	4					8	What?! You're telling me that thing's a\nthermonuclear device?\n
1	en	246	0xf6dc0	63196	5					8	Do they have any idea what kind of destruction\nthat thing would cause...?\n
1	en	246	0xf6dc0	63196	6					8	I know, it's crazy. I mean, even overkill has its\nlimits.\n
1	en	246	0xf6dc0	63196	7					8	If it's strategic value they want, they could have\ngone with something smaller.\n
