1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	7	9473	10992	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	The explosion was seen as far off as Finland - 600\nmiles away\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	8	11006	11842	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	- and some people even reported windows\nshattering.\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	9	11870	12803	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	The shockwave traveled three times around the\nearth.\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	10	12803	13221	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	Three times?\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	11	13221	14238	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	Peace Walker is armed with a massive hydrogen\nbomb\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	12	14238	14976	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	even more destructive than Tsar Bomba.\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	13	14976	15868	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	It can sneak into enemy territory, lie low,\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	14	15882	17428	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	and - in the event of an enemy nuclear strike -\ndetonate itself in retaliation.\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	15	17526	18306	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	And the locomotion system that lets it do that...\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	16	18306	18780	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	...My research...\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	17	18780	20006	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	...Snake, those legs were supposed to make my\ndream come true.\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	18	20006	21413	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	Now they're about to jump the fence of nuclear\ndeterrence. You have to stop them!\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	19	21413	22736	0x0ea8e31c	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	I'll apply all my energy into developing weapons and\nequipment to help you do it.\n
1	en	247	0xf7300	63280	20	22736	23224	0x0e28dce6	v_bri_huy0080_020_1	21	Sounds like a deal.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	0					21	What made you put an AI into Peace Walker?\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	1					21	Well, for one thing, because it can't be manned.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	2					21	Peace Walker's designed to enter enemy territory\nand blow itself up - if necessary.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	3					21	You can't put a person inside a weapon that could\nblow at anytime, can you?\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	4					21	So we equipped it with an AI instead.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	5					21	That's... strangely humane of you.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	6					21	And besides, Peace Walker was designed as a\nbipedal weapons system.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	7					21	You can't imagine how hard it shakes when it\nwalks. It'd turn a man into mush.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	8					21	Plus, when launching a nuclear missile,\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	9					21	it has to perform ballistic calculations in real time,\nsee?\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	10					21	Because it's always moving.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	11					21	Hold on. If that's all it does, then a\nhigh-performance computer ought to do the job.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	12					21	It doesn't need intelligence.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	13					21	That's a very good point, Snake. Which brings me\nto the real reason...\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	14					21	Peace Walker needs AI to make decisions\nregarding nuclear retaliation.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	15					21	It's what ensures perfectly mutual assured\ndestruction.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	16					21	I've heard all of this before. You want a war\nbetween machines?\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	17					21	We'd never actually launch the first nuke, of\ncourse.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	18					21	It's strictly a counterattack system.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	19					21	Only a politician could make such an illogical\ndecision as starting a nuclear war.\n
1	en	247	0xf7a40	63396	20					21	Conversely, if an adversary launches a nuke at us,\nthe AI will not fail to retaliate.\n
