1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	0				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	Those papers the CIA gave you... Was there any\ndata on the Shagohod in there?\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	1				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	Shagohod?\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	2				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	A nuclear tank that launches IRBMs.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	3				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	It competed against Granin's system for approval.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	4				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	Oh, the thing with the rockets. Designed by a guy\nnamed... Sokolov, right? ...Heh heh.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	5				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	What's so funny?\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	6				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	No, I was just remembering some of the\n"commentary" Granin added to the Shagohod\npapers.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	7				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	You should have seen the way he bad-mouthed it.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	8				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	It was too conservative, too ugly...\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	9				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	I can imagine.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	10				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	He was so angry when he wrote that he smeared\nup the ink.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	11				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	And you know how shoddy the paper is over there\nto begin with.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	12				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	...I'll bet. That's Granin, all right.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	13				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	Imagine, accelerating the launcher itself to 300\nmiles an hour to extend the range of an IRBM...\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	14				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	As stupid as it sounds, it's a hell of a concept.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	15				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	Who but the Soviets would think of using a tank as\nthe first stage of a rocket?\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	16				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	I actually took a cue from the Shagohod when I\ndeveloped the Pupa.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	17				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	That hovercraft thing? You stole that one, too?\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	18				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	Give me a little credit! I only borrowed the concept.\nThe technology is original.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	19				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	As it turned out,\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	20				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	hover technology wasn't enough to handle all the\nterrain in Central America.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	21				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	It relied too much on brute force.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	22				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	But the Shagohod was a major threat.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	23				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	That thing could corner like you wouldn't believe -\nbuilt pretty tough, too.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	24				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	You sure know a lot about it.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	25				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	It almost did me in. I couldn't forget it if I tried.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	26				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	Did you in? ...So you were the one who took it\ndown!\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	27				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	Wow! You really are amazing.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	28				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	I didn't do it alone.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	29				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	No, seriously, thank you.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	30				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	We might not be here today if they'd begun\nmass-producing that thing.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	31				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	Then again, they're hard at work now miniaturizing\nnuclear warheads.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	32				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	Pretty soon they won't even need an accelerated\nlauncher like the Shagohod.\n
1	en	251	0xfb280	64296	33				v_bri_huy0140_000_0	34	Great. That means they're that much closer to\nbeing able to launch from anywhere in the world.\n
1	en	251	0xfbe10	64481	0					7	Chico called Peace Walker the basilisco.\n
1	en	251	0xfbe10	64481	1					7	Basilisco? ...Oh, right, Spanish.\n
1	en	251	0xfbe10	64481	2					7	That's funny.\n
1	en	251	0xfbe10	64481	3					7	I once used the codename Basilisk for the Peace\nWalker platform myself.\n
1	en	251	0xfbe10	64481	4					7	What for?\n
1	en	251	0xfbe10	64481	5					7	The class of lizards called basilisks can walk atop\nany type of terrain.\n
1	en	251	0xfbe10	64481	6					7	In a pinch, they can even stand up on two legs and\nrun across water.\n
1	en	251	0xfbe10	64481	7					7	Perfect name for a system that can walk anywhere\nin Cent�
