1	en	260	0x104860	66694	0					27	I spoke out against her going,\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	1					27	submitting a report stating the ray shielding was\ninadequate.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	2					27	But the brass's response was brusque:\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	3					27	"She's already been exposed to a nuclear test in\nNevada. She's the perfect candidate."\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	4					27	It was completely irrational.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	5					27	Repeated exposure to radiation would only\nincrease the danger.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	6					27	But the government was still reeling from the\nSoviets' success with Sputnik.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	7					27	There was no hope of getting a rational response.\nThey were simply too panicked.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	8					27	People can be so obtuse when it comes to things\nthey can't see.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	9					27	I, however, understood all too well.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	10					27	Just as invisible ultraviolet radiation scorched my\nskin,\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	11					27	heavy particle radiation from space would cause\nirreparable harm to human tissue.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	12					27	In a word, she was expendable.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	13					27	It was during The Boss's pre-flight checkup\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	14					27	that I noticed something strange on the X-ray of\nher skull.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	15					27	Part of the right hemisphere of her brain was\ndamaged.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	16					27	It seemed inexplicable given her keen intelligence\nand amazing physical prowess.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	17					27	But there it was, and I decided to report it.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	18					27	I hoped that perhaps my discovery of a physical\ndefect\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	19					27	would result in the flight being canceled.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	20					27	...But as I went to make my report, she stopped me.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	21					27	"Why?" I demanded. "How can you let yourself be\ntheir guinea pig?!"\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	22					27	Ignoring my protests, she took me up to the roof\nof the lab.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	23					27	The night sky was ablaze with stars.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	24					27	It was there that I learned how she had wounded\nher head.\n
1	en	260	0x104860	66694	25					27	1943, Los Alamos.\n
