1	en	265	0x109080	67848	0				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Enter simulation date.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	1				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	August 24.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	2				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Location?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	3				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Tselinoyarsk, USSR.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	4				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Mission?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	5				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Support a covert agent whose objective is the\nrescue of a nuclear weapons scientist.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	6				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Who is the agent?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	7				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Your student. Your... most beloved...\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	8				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	...Acknowledged. Define current mission progress.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	9				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	With your help, the agent has successfully made\ncontact with the target.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	10				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	All that's left is to wait for recovery.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	11				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Now, deduce the best course of action.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	12				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	...I take the scientist away from the agent.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	13				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	What for?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	14				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	As a gift when I defect.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	15				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	...Why are you defecting?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	16				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	To reform my Special Forces unit with my former\ncomrades-in-arms.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	17				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	NO! I don't want to know your objective. I'm asking\nfor the reason.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	18				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Why are you betraying your country?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	19				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	...I do not defect in order to betray America.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	20				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Betrayal is merely the outcome of that defection.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	21				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Response time is always slower here...\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	22				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Perhaps she lacks confidence in her judgment.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	23				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	You're a hero in the West. Why should the Soviets\ntrust you?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	24				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	In addition to the scientist,\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	25				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	I provide them with a portable nuclear warhead\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	26				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	in order to win the favor of a Russian GRU officer.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	27				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	...And then you launched it.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	28				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Launched... the nuke? Me?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	29				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	That's right. At a target inside Soviet territory.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	30				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Nuclear weapons... make my blood run cold. They\nblot out the future. How... could I...?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	31				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Karma... Is... is it my karma?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	32				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	The karma my mistake has brought upon us... My...\nMy...\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	33				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Attention. Discontinue forward reasoning.\nCross-check with knowledge base.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	34				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Affirmative.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	35				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	...Cross-check complete. Revising conclusion as\nfollows:\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	36				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	I steal the new weapons developed by the scientist\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	37				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	and then launch the nuke at the weapons design\nbureau.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	38				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Forward and backward reasoning are in conflict...\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	39				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Attention. Return to forward reasoning.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	40				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Affirmative.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	41				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	...Your apprentice returns for the scientist.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	42				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	I send him away.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	43				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	He doesn't give up.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	44				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	I send my comrades to defeat him.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	45				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	All of them fail.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	46				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Even the GRU officer who oversaw your defection\nis defeated by your apprentice\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	47				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	- along with the new weapon.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	48				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Now, what is your course of action?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	49				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	...I fight him.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	50				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Why? With your GRU patron dead, there's no\nreason for you to fight.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	51				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Why not just run away?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	52				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	I... must fight him.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	53				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	I do not see the reason. With a solider of your\ncaliber on his side,\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	54				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	how could the GRU officer be defeated to begin\nwith? Did you betray him, too?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	55				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	I... I've been waiting... for a long time.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	56				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	You could switch allegiance from GRU to KGB,\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	57				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	and take the remaining nuke as a gift.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	58				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	There's no chance they wouldn't welcome a hero\nof your stature.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	59				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Drift away. My place is with them now.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	60				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	I didn't ask you that! Give me the basis for your\nreasoning! Tell me the truth...\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	61				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Politics determine who you face on the battlefield.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	62				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Why won't you answer me?! It's like you were just\nwaiting for him to kill you!\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	63				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	I was disloyal... Betrayed my country... I deserve to\ndie...\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	64				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	How can you say that?! You can't be a traitor!\nYou're not that kind of person!\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	65				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Kill me... Kill me now...\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	66				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	STOP IT! STOP IT! Attention! Discontinue reasoning!!\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	67				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	One must die, and one must live...\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	68				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Stop it, damn you! DISCONTINUE!\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	69				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Life's end... Isn't it beautiful...?\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	70				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	SHUT DOWN!!\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	71				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	...Always in the same place, her reasoning goes\nhaywire.\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	72				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	Someone holds the key... Perhaps it's him...\n
1	en	265	0x109080	67848	73				v_dsl_cst_0040_000_0	74	I'll get it out of him. One way or another...!\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	0				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	As of today I will be living here at Mother Base.\nNow my real trial begins.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	1				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	Zadornov was paying my room, board, and tuition,\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	2				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	but he has since been captured.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	3				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	I told the man that with no more money from the\nKGB,\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	4				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	I could no longer afford school.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	5				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	...He bought my story, and when I said I would be\nwilling to work,\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	6				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	he took pity on me and let me stay.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	7				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	For some reason Miller really plead my case.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	8				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	That was helpful, but the man is still a fool.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	9				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	His men are no better.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	10				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	They think their training makes them strong,\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	11				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	but that kind of strength is nothing in the face of\ntrue power.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	12				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	And better yet, they wait on me hand and foot,\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	13				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	believing I am just a schoolgirl.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	14				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	Looks like I won't be working too hard, after all.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	15				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	Just today,\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	16				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	while scouting out the living quarters,\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	17				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	I saw a group of them in the corner of the deck\nmaking a fuss.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	18				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	Going over for a look, I saw they were feeding a\nkitten.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	19				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	A bunch of grown, hard men, and they are the\nones acting like schoolgirls!\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	20				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	"Look, isn't he cute?" What is wrong with them?\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	21				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	Disgusted, I just nodded and smiled.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	22				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	I must stay in character, after all.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	23				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	I indulged their chit-chat for a few moments,\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	24				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	then one of them asked me to give the thing a\nname.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	25				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	They had just taken it from its mother.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	26				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	I named it Nuke.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	27				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	I improvised some nonsense about how\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	28				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	"our compassion for living things can help prevent\nwars."\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	29				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	The men gave me a little fish.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	30				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	I held it out in my palm, and the kitten happily ate\nit up.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	31				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	What a pathetic... feeble creature.\n
1	en	266	0x10a6e0	68206	32				v_paz_dry_0010_000_0	33	It sickens me.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	0				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	Today Chico invited me to go fishing with the\nsoldiers.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	1				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	I suppose finding one's own food does have its\nmerit,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	2				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	but I prefer not to be involved in such a degrading\ntask.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	3				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	And their prattling on about fishing being "fun" is\nnonsense.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	4				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	I'm not here to find playmates.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	5				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	Nevertheless, distasteful as it was,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	6				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	I went along in order to maintain my cover.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	7				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	Chico thrust a fishing pole into my hands, and we\nwent up onto the deck,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	8				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	where several soldiers had gathered.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	9				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	They welcomed us warmly.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	10				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	With so few women aboard Mother Base, I'm\ntreated like a princess.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	11				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	No one suspects I'm neither a teenager nor a\nstudent.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	12				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	It was nice and sunny,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	13				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	with a gentle breeze and waves.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	14				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	As I cast my line and waited for a bite,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	15				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	the soldiers began to ask me all sorts of questions.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	16				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	As always,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	17				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	I answered according to our pre-defined scenario,\nfeigning a smile.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	18				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	As I sat there feeding them lies, the fish began to\nbite,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	19				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	and the soldiers began to focus on their prey.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	20				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	Chico had his bait stolen by a fish,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	21				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	and got so angry that he stood up and nearly fell\ninto the sea.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	22				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	Everybody laughed.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	23				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	It almost made me want to join in, too.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	24				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	At some point, I got a bite myself.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	25				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	The instant after I felt that first gentle tug,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	26				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	the fish yanked the line with astonishing strength,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	27				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	and I let out a cry of surprise.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	28				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	I thought it was going to be huge.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	29				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	It was my first time fishing, and I was a bit\nflustered,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	30				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	so the soldier beside me helped by supporting the\npole from behind.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	31				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	"Reel it in!" they shouted.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	32				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	I nodded, turning the handle as fast as I could.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	33				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	I wondered what kind of fish live below the surface,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	34				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	and thought back to the deep-sea dives I had to\ndo as part of training.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	35				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	Those were difficult days,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	36				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	but I remember finding the multi-colored fish\ngliding through the water incredibly soothing.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	37				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	After a hard fight, I pulled it up. To my surprise,\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	38				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	it wasn't even half a vara (16 in). Rather\nanti-climactic.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	39				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	But I wasn't doing it for fun, so I wasn't the least\nbit disappointed.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	40				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	Nuke was hovering nearby with an expectant look\non his face, so I gave the fish to him.\n
1	en	267	0x10b0e0	68366	41				v_paz_dry_0020_000_0	42	All in all, a thoroughly wasted day.\n
1	en	267	0x10be70	68583	0					2	Preparations are coming along nicely.\n
1	en	267	0x10be70	68583	1					2	No one suspects me of being the one to let\nZadornov out of his cell.\n
