1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	0					17	Every month,\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	1					17	Mother Base throws a party for all the soldiers\nwhose birthdays fall in that month.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	2					17	There's something strange about a military\norganization having parties.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	3					17	Really, though, it is just an excuse to drink and\nmake noise.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	4					17	It is not easy to get alcohol on a fortress in the\nmiddle of the ocean.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	5					17	Most days they are training from dawn till dusk.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	6					17	They do not have time for things like drinking.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	7					17	That is why Snake and Miller came up with the\nidea - to give everyone a chance to let loose.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	8					17	Obviously, a bunch of boors like that are not going\nto bother with blowing out candles on a cake.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	9					17	Rather, they sit there in a cloud of cigarette\nsmoke,\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	10					17	drink beer, eat meat, tell tasteless jokes and swap\ncrude insults about one another's hometowns.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	11					17	But it hardly ever breaks out into something\nserious.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	12					17	They talk up a storm, but they're just having fun.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	13					17	It is funny. You've got members of FSLN rubbing\nshoulders with the UCLAs.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	14					17	People who once would have considered the other\nmortal enemies.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	15					17	I wonder if that is what makes Big Boss so popular.\n
1	en	272	0x110ab0	69803	16					17	In leaving their countries behind, they leave their\nhatred for other countries, too.\n
