1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	0					46	She told me everything.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	1					46	Why did she open her heart to me like that?\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	2					46	At the time, I couldn't understand it.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	3					46	But now I think I do.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	4					46	Snake...\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	5					46	she wanted you to know the truth\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	6					46	She chose me to tell you.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	7					46	That's why she saved my life.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	8					46	I've lied to you so many times. But not this time.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	9					46	My orders from the government were to obtain the\nLegacy...\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	10					46	...and to eliminate everyone who knew the truth\nabout what happened.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	11					46	In other words, I'm supposed to kill you.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	12					46	But I can't do it.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	13					46	Not because we loved each other.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	14					46	And not because you saved my life.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	15					46	But because I made a promise to The Boss...\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	16					46	And I intend to keep it.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	17					46	I just wanted you to know.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	18					46	And...\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	19					46	you have to live.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	20					46	Snake, listen to me.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	21					46	She didn't betray the United States.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	22					46	No, far from it. She was a hero who died for her\ncountry.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	23					46	She carried out her mission knowing full well what\nwas going to happen.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	24					46	Self-sacrifice... because that was her duty.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	25					46	The Boss' defection was a ruse set up by the U.S.\ngovernment.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	26					46	It was all a big drama staged by Washington\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	27					46	so they could get their hands on the Philosophers'\nLegacy.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	28					46	And The Boss was the star of the show.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	29					46	They planned it so that they could get the Legacy\nthat Colonel Volgin inherited...\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	30					46	...and destroy the Shagohod at the same time.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	31					46	Only a legendary hero like The Boss could have\nearned Volgin's trust.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	32					46	Finding out where the Philosophers' Legacy was\nhidden was to be her greatest mission.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	33					46	Everything was going according to plan...\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	34					46	But then something happened that no one could\nhave predicted.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	35					46	Colonel Volgin fired an American-made nuclear\nwarhead at Sokolov's research facility.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	36					46	Khrushchev demanded that the U.S. government\nprovide proof that it wasn't involved...\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	37					46	They couldn't just abort the operation to steal the\nLegacy.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	38					46	So the operation itself was greatly expanded and\nrevised.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	39					46	The authorities in Washington knew that in order\nto prove its innocence,\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	40					46	it had to get rid of The Boss...\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	41					46	...and that one of their own would have to do the\njob.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	42					46	The public couldn't be allowed to find out about it...\nnot ever.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	43					46	This, they concluded, would be the best way to\nkeep the whole thing under wraps.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	44					46	The Boss wouldn't be allowed to come back home\nalive.\n
1	en	276	0x1145f0	70751	45					46	And she wouldn't be allowed to kill herself.\n
