2	en	901	0x385620	230754	0					34	How's that map, Snake? Think you can\nuse it?\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	1					34	It tells me where their bases are, but it's\njust a bunch of points.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	2					34	No routes. I need better intel on the lay\nof the land.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	3					34	Snake, the "professor" said he's got the\nSandinistas on his side.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	4					34	Said you should get in touch with the\nFSLN comandante.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	5					34	Do they know they're backed by KGB?\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	6					34	Nah... As far as they know they're really\nfighting for the revolution.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	7					34	The KGB is staying behind the scenes.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	8					34	I'm not sure the Sandinistas are aware of\nwhat's really going on.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	9					34	Still can't believe anybody'd bring nukes\nhere...\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	10					34	Yeah, that's a shocker.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	11					34	Costa Rica's party to the Tlatelolco\nTreaty,\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	12					34	which declares Latin America a nuke-free\nzone.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	13					34	Based on Japan's Three Non-Nuclear\nPrinciples,\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	14					34	it bans the testing, use, import, or\ndeployment of nuclear weapons.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	15					34	If word of this gets out, OPANAL will be\nforced to act.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	16					34	It'll cause an international uproar.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	17					34	The Treaty was signed to prevent\nanother Cuban Missile Crisis.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	18					34	If the U.S. itself is going to scrap it...\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	19					34	Latin America's too close to spawning\nanother Cuba or two already.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	20					34	The entire continent would become one\nbig powder keg.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	21					34	Well... If they did bring nukes, we can't let\nthem get away with it.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	22					34	Are they planning a test? Showing off?\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	23					34	Or is it all to keep the anti-American\nmovement in check?\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	24					34	Good question. Why bring them here? I\ncan't figure it out.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	25					34	Whatever the CIA's up to in Costa Rica,\nthe "professor" wants it stopped.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	26					34	We need to find out what that something\nis.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	27					34	We need to get ready first, Kaz. Repairs?\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	28					34	Working as fast as we can, Boss. This\nplace is pretty beat... It looks like hell.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	29					34	But as long as you're with us, we'll make\nit heaven.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	30					34	No one can bother us here. No state\ntelling us what to do.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	31					34	This is the MSF's haven, our Mother Base.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	32					34	And with this foothold, we'll back you up\neven better than before.\n
2	en	901	0x385620	230754	33					34	We're gonna turn this pile of junk into\nsomething big.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	0					57	Snake, I rigged that radio so you can\ncontact our young lady friend Paz.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	1					57	Is she OK?\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	2					57	No need to worry. She's tougher than you\nthink...\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	3					57	Still just a kid.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	4					57	Which is exactly why she could be an\neffective source of information.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	5					57	Besides, that little ángel de la paz is the\none who gave us this mission, right?\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	6					57	...I guess.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	7					57	I'll put her on.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	8					57	Snake...\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	9					57	Paz. Where are you?\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	10					57	Ciudad Colón. A school. The teacher told\nme to stay here until things quiet down.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	11					57	Teacher? Oh, him. He's... Yeah, that's\nprobably good advice.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	12					57	Si. He has a radio in his room, so we can\ntalk anytime.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	13					57	...Pretty fancy for a teacher.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	14					57	Promise me, Snake, that you'll bring back\npeace. And...\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	15					57	I know. I'll contact you if I find your friend.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	16					57	Thank you. Snake, if you need to know\nabout Costa Rica\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	17					57	- the geography, the climate, the wildlife,\nanything - just ask me.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	18					57	I know about its history and laws, too. We\nlearned it all in school.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	19					57	Got it. I have a question, I'll ask.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	20					57	...I, uh...\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	21					57	What?\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	22					57	In school I also learned that peace is an\nunnatural state for human society.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	23					57	And that war is a constant threat to our\nrelationships with others.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	24					57	That's right.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	25					57	So, to achieve peace, we have to create\nit ourselves.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	26					57	Crying about it won't bring it about, or\nmake it last.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	27					57	Each one of us must go and seek it out.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	28					57	You won't find it without making sacrifices.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	29					57	No offense, but I don't know what peace\nis.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	30					57	Never felt what it's like. Never even been\ninterested in it.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	31					57	Snake...?\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	32					57	Ah, sorry.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	33					57	Listen Paz, I think your ideas are...\nadmirable, and I hope they turn out to be\nright.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	34					57	Yeah, me too.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	35					57	Peace is in your name. Who better to\nhelp bring it back?\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	36					57	Thanks, Snake. I will be here whenever\nyou need me. See you later.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	37					57	Snake, use your radio to call people.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	38					57	But stay alert.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	39					57	You're in the middle of a mission, and\ncan't afford to let your guard down.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	40					57	Got it.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	41					57	Need to know more about Costa Rica?\nPaz can help you out.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	42					57	Good to know.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	43					57	We'll follow their transport route. That\nshould take us straight to their main base.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	44					57	From what I've seen, it looks like nukes.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	45					57	Agreed.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	46					57	The key thing now is to confirm whether\nthose "spears" really are what we think\nthey are, and if so, why they're here.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	47					57	Follow the transport route, find the nukes.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	48					57	That's what I'm thinking.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	49					57	First, we should make contact with the\nSandinista comandante.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	50					57	They can tell us more about what's up\nahead.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	51					57	But it looks like their hideout's already\ncome under attack.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	52					57	We'd better hope they're still alive.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	53					57	Snake, infiltrate that cabin and secure\nthe Sandinistas' comandante.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	54					57	Neutralize any guards by knocking them\nout,\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	55					57	putting them to sleep, or even using the\nFulton recovery system.\n
2	en	902	0x3861c0	230940	56					57	You choose how to handle it, Boss.\n
2	en	903	0x387380	231224	0					12	Snake, what was that thing?!\n
2	en	903	0x387380	231224	1	821	1532	0x0e28dce6		12	Whatever it was, it looked unmanned.\n
2	en	903	0x387380	231224	2	1602	2716	0x0e463a34		12	Unmanned? I'd heard rumors, but an\noperational unit...?\n
2	en	903	0x387380	231224	3	2716	3274	0x0e28dce6		12	What the hell is going on here?\n
2	en	903	0x387380	231224	4	3315	4820	0x0e463a34		12	Not to quote Amanda, but the hardware\nthey've got here isn't just unusual, it's\noverkill.\n
2	en	903	0x387380	231224	5	4876	6227	0x0e463a34		12	Which means one thing: it's nukes. So the\nquestion now becomes, why?\n
2	en	903	0x387380	231224	6	6227	7174	0x0e28dce6		12	We can't make that call yet. We need\nmore intel.\n
2	en	903	0x387380	231224	7	7244	7885	0x0e463a34		12	How? Our source is dead.\n
2	en	903	0x387380	231224	8	8052	8554	0x0e28dce6		12	But his daughter isn't.\n
2	en	903	0x387380	231224	9	8609	9264	0x0e463a34		12	Good thinking. We can follow her...\n
2	en	903	0x387380	231224	10	9362	10602	0x0e463a34		12	Head for that the next outpost, and make\ncontact with Amanda... if she's still alive.\n
2	en	903	0x387380	231224	11	10616	10866	0x0e28dce6		12	Roger.\n
2	en	903	0x387770	231287	0					3	The direction Amanda's Sandinistas were\ngoing\n
2	en	903	0x387770	231287	1					3	corresponds to the location of the next\noutpost, a supply depot.\n
2	en	903	0x387770	231287	2					3	We should be able to make contact with\nher there.\n
2	en	903	0x3878d0	231309	0					2	That's an armored vehicle unit, Snake.\n
2	en	903	0x3878d0	231309	1					2	Either destroy the vehicle or neutralize\nthe soldiers. Take it out!\n
2	en	903	0x3879e0	231326	0					16	Snake, Amanda's reached the plant.\n
2	en	903	0x3879e0	231326	1	1017	1281	0x0e3bb338		16	Snake...\n
2	en	903	0x3879e0	231326	2	1462	2117	0x0e28dce6		16	Amanda, how do you feel?\n
2	en	903	0x3879e0	231326	3	2229	3705	0x0e3bb338		16	Some first helicopter ride. I'll be perfectly\nhappy if it's my last.\n
2	en	903	0x3879e0	231326	4	3817	4444	0x0e463a34		16	As you can see, she's doing fine.\n
2	en	903	0x3879e0	231326	5	4486	5879	0x0e463a34		16	I set Amanda up with her own frequency,\nso call her anytime you need to.\n
2	en	903	0x3879e0	231326	6	5935	8317	0x0e3bb338		16	If you have any questions about American\nbases or mercenary units, or about el\nFrente, just ask.\n
