2	en	904	0x388570	231511	0					50	Snake, Chico made it over.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	1					50	Snake!\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	2					50	Chico, you made it.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	3					50	Made it?! Don't give me that!\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	4					50	You say you're gonna give me a new life,\nand then you nearly kill me?!\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	5					50	I take it you didn't enjoy the trip?\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	6					50	What's the big idea, dragging me off in a...\nballoon!\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	7					50	I might as well have taken a colibri!\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	8					50	At least you got a nice view. Or are you\nafraid of heights?\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	9					50	Whatever. I just wish you'd explained it to\nme first.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	10					50	Would you have agreed to go if I did?\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	11					50	Thank you for saving us, Snake.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	12					50	Amanda, a word of advice.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	13					50	What?\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	14					50	Stop treating him like a child.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	15					50	Yes... yes, I know. You're right. I shouldn't.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	16					50	Amanda, you're coming back after your\nleg heals, right?\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	17					50	Of course. We still have work to do.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	18					50	"We," huh... Are you sure you've got\nChico's future in mind when you say that?\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	19					50	What do you mean? We're sworn to our\nfather's cause, to helping the revolution\nsucceed.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	20					50	Revolution or no revolution, you pick up a\ngun, and sooner or later you're going to\nhell.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	21					50	Are you prepared for that?\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	22					50	I am. If the alternative is giving up the\ncountry I love, I'll take hell.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	23					50	Really... Well then, you're going to have to\nstop treating Chico like a brother\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	24					50	and start treating him like a soldier.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	25					50	I ...You're right.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	26					50	...Welcome to hell.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	27					50	Snake, can I ask you a favor?\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	28					50	Shoot.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	29					50	You find any prisoners from el Frente,\nyou bring 'em back alive. 'Cause...\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	30					50	You trying to make amends for talking?\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	31					50	Not just that. Because they're compas...\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	32					50	All right. But first I've gotta catch up to\nthat cargo.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	33					50	I'll do whatever I can to help.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	34					50	Call me if there's anything you need to\nknow about the area. And...\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	35					50	And what?\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	36					50	Let me know if you encounter any wildlife\nyou've never seen before.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	37					50	Never seen before? What, like that\nbasilisco you were talking about?\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	38					50	I'm talking about UMAs.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	39					50	U... M... As?\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	40					50	Y'know, like ancient dinosaurs or\nlegendary monsters.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	41					50	One day, I'm going to be a hunter.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	42					50	Is that right. OK, sure.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	43					50	If you wanna know more, I'm happy to tell\nyou!\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	44					50	Right. I'll be in touch, Chico.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	45					50	OK, Snake. The enemy's cargo is headed\nfor the next outpost, a rail terminal.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	46					50	Chico says no one's ever set foot past\nthere.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	47					50	Their main base is probably on the other\nside of that tunnel.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	48					50	Unless we catch those spears before\nreaching it, they'll be in enemy hands.\n
2	en	904	0x388570	231511	49					50	You've got to stop them. Hurry, Snake.\n
2	en	905	0x3894b0	231755	0					4	Snake, according to Chico, the nuclear\nmaterials will be loaded from a train and\non to a truck\n
2	en	905	0x3894b0	231755	1					4	at a rail terminal near the eastern foot of\nIrazú.\n
2	en	905	0x3894b0	231755	2					4	If we can't cut 'em off at that terminal,\nwe'll be in a world of hurt.\n
2	en	905	0x3894b0	231755	3					4	Hurry, Snake!\n
2	en	905	0x389670	231783	0					2	Snake! That's an enemy tank unit.\n
2	en	905	0x389670	231783	1					2	Either neutralize the soldiers or destroy\nthe tank. Get 'em!\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	0					40	Snake, the truck is headed up the\nmountain road past the tunnel.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	1					40	So it was nukes after all.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	2					40	What now? Their main base is up ahead.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	3					40	I better hurry after 'em, then.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	4					40	But...\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	5					40	Kaz, if I don't get moving it'll be too late!\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	6					40	All right.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	7					40	I guess you never let dangerous\nassignments or risk aversion get in your\nway.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	8					40	How do I get inside the mountain? I can\nforget about the tunnel.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	9					40	Yeah, the tank took care of that...\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	10					40	Any other routes?\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	11					40	Why don't I let a local expert take over?\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	12					40	Snake, you need a way into the mountain?\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	13					40	Yeah. Got one?\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	14					40	Let's see... You remember that prison I\nwas in?\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	15					40	In the village, right?\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	16					40	Right. Go back to the village and head\nnorth.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	17					40	There's a bridge that connects to the\nmountain road.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	18					40	It crosses over a gorge. That's probably\nthe best way...\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	19					40	But there is a little problem.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	20					40	The path heading north from the village\nis barricaded.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	21					40	You might have to break through...\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	22					40	Got it.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	23					40	The heart of Irazú...\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	24					40	That's where the enemy's base has got\nto be, Snake. And maybe...\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	25					40	Let me guess - the basilisco?\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	26					40	You don't believe me, do you?\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	27					40	No, I mean... We'll have to see.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	28					40	Snake, Irazú features a number of crater\nlakes.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	29					40	The Oduber government had planned to\nuse those lakes\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	30					40	to construct hydroelectric plants as one\nof its big state development projects.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	31					40	The project was scrapped,\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	32					40	but there's still a small opening at the\nbottom of the lake.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	33					40	Meaning?\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	34					40	I checked the satellite imagery, but didn't\nsee anything man-made.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	35					40	Which means they've probably built a\nbase inside the mountain...\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	36					40	Could just be a storage igloo for\nexplosives, or maybe some kind of\nresearch facility.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	37					40	What do they hope to accomplish by\nbringing the nukes there?\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	38					40	First things first. Get past that barricade\nnorth of the village.\n
2	en	905	0x389770	231799	39					40	Looks like the only way through is the\nnoisy way - you'll have to blow it up.\n
