2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	1					54	Huey, your ID card isn't working.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	2					54	It won't open the lock!\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	3					54	...It can't be...\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	4					54	What's going on?!\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	5					54	She hates me that much?!\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	6					54	...Strangelove's in charge of authorizing\nIDs.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	7					54	Sometimes a working card has its\nprivileges removed.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	8					54	...Say, if she decides she doesn't like that\ncard's carrier.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	9					54	You think that's what happened?\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	10					54	Well, I was never exactly her favorite.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	11					54	Well, this could be tricky.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	12					54	The soldiers outside aren't allowed in the\nlab either, so their cards won't do you\nany good...\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	13					54	Great...\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	14					54	Snake.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	15					54	Kaz, where's Cecile?\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	16					54	She just got here. Hold on.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	17					54	Snake!\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	18					54	Cecile. How'd it feel to fly?\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	19					54	Wonderful. For a moment, I felt what it\nmust be like to be a bird.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	20					54	It almost made me want to give up my\nresearch and get a pilot's license...\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	21					54	Did you need something?\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	22					54	You said you'd gotten an ID card, right?\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	23					54	Yes. But it was confiscated when the\nguards caught me.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	24					54	Who took it?! What'd he look like?!\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	25					54	He had on an orange jacket.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	26					54	I... cannot recall his face, though.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	27					54	Yeah, they all look pretty much the same.\nWhere did it happen?\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	28					54	Let me think...\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	29					54	Ah, yes! I do remember hearing the song\nof a nearby quetzal.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	30					54	Just what I'd expect from a birder.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	31					54	Would you like to hear it?\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	32					54	Hmm? What's that song?\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	33					54	It's my quetzal. I took it with me when I\nwas rescued.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	34					54	Didn't you say something about them\nbeing covered under the Washington\nConvention...\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	35					54	Just kidding. That was just me... an\nimitation.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	36					54	An essential skill for any ornithologist.\nPretty good, no?\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	37					54	Damn good.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	38					54	If you want to hear the quetzal's song\nagain, just let me know.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	39					54	I can tell you all about the birds of Costa\nRica, too.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	40					54	Yeah... will do. Thanks, Cecile.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	41					54	No, no, thank you, Snake. Talk to you\nsoon.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	42					54	Kaz, did you play that tape for Cecile?\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	43					54	I sure did. It's hers, all right.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	44					54	Then she must be...\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	45					54	She's not. Cecile says she's never even\nmet Paz.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	46					54	What?\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	47					54	She's at least 10 years too old.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	48					54	But...\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	49					54	I'm guessing Paz convinced herself that it\nwas the tape her friend made.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	50					54	But never mind that. Let's go over what\nwe know so far.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	51					54	The soldier with the ID card is wearing an\norange jacket\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	52					54	and is in a location where you'll hear\nquetzals singing.\n
2	en	907	0x38b170	232215	53					54	Find that soldier. Retrieve that card.\n
2	en	908	0x38c0c0	232460	0					4	Snake, to gain access to the lab you'll\nneed an ID card.\n
2	en	908	0x38c0c0	232460	1					4	You can get one from a guard in an\norange jacket stationed in an area where\nyou can hear quetzals singing.\n
2	en	908	0x38c0c0	232460	2					4	To get the ID card from the soldier, do a\nbody check.\n
2	en	908	0x38c0c0	232460	3					4	You've got to get inside that lab before\nthe AI gets shipped out. Get a move on!\n
2	en	908	0x38c2c0	232492	0					2	Snake, that's the Chrysalis weapon Huey\nwas referring to.\n
2	en	908	0x38c2c0	232492	1					2	You know what to do!\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	0					59	Snake...\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	1					59	She played me like a piano...\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	2					59	Forget about it. You'll get 'em back.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	3					59	That is, as long as you've got the will to\ndo it.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	4					59	I'm not giving up.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	5					59	All right, then...\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	6					59	I confirmed the location with Huey.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	7					59	The final testing base for Peace Walker is\n15 miles to the north of that lab.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	8					59	It's an underground facility disguised as a\nrock quarry.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	9					59	All you need to do is sneak in and\ndestroy the AI for good this time.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	10					59	Right.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	11					59	Snake, you can destroy it, right?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	12					59	Yeah.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	13					59	We all have our limits - actions beyond\nour abilities.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	14					59	Don't worry. I won't screw it up this time.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	15					59	You're the one who killed The Boss.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	16					59	Destroying that AI means reliving that\nmemory.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	17					59	It's just a machine.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	18					59	Snake, I'm worried.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	19					59	Worried?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	20					59	For the same reason the CIA entrusted\nthe nuclear launch to an AI.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	21					59	A man can condemn a handful of\ncriminals to the death penalty\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	22					59	if they're prepared to assume that\nresponsibility.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	23					59	But who among us could do the same to\nhundreds of millions of innocent civilians?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	24					59	Who could reduce thousands of years of\nhuman history to ash in an instant?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	25					59	Could any flesh-and-blood human being\nmake that decision?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	26					59	No way in hell.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	27					59	No one man could bear the burden of\ntotal genocide.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	28					59	It's what's allowed our cowardly species\nto survive all this time.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	29					59	But for a machine, willpower is no issue.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	30					59	What are you saying, Kaz?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	31					59	You're a hero, Snake. But you're not a\nmachine.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	32					59	That I can't destroy that thing?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	33					59	That machine's not the problem. It's that\nThe Boss still lives - inside of you.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	34					59	Bullshit!\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	35					59	She's dead, Snake. It's time to come to\nterms with that.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	36					59	Let me put it another way.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	37					59	You've left everything behind - your\ncountry, your identity, your past and\nideals...\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	38					59	But there's still one thing you haven't let\ngo of.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	39					59	What are you talking about?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	40					59	The Boss. You still haven't let her go.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	41					59	That's why you're so afraid to find out\nthe truth about her.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	42					59	And that's what's holding you back from\nyour future.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	43					59	Snake, she died a decade ago.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	44					59	How long can you live with a ghost?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	45					59	Kaz, I thought I knew everything about\nher.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	46					59	But I still don't understand what\nhappened to her at the end.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	47					59	There you are no different from that\nscientist woman.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	48					59	When she didn't believe me, I realized\nsomething.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	49					59	That debriefing I heard could've been part\nof the cover story they made up.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	50					59	Now even I'm not sure what her real\nintentions were.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	51					59	Why did she take that mission?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	52					59	How did she feel about dying?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	53					59	Why was I chosen?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	54					59	You want to know the truth?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	55					59	The truth won't change the past. You still\nwant to know?\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	56					59	...No. I took on this mission for a kid who\nbelieves in peace.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	57					59	Hm. Fine, then. There's no point in\narguing. Peace Walker is on the verge of\ncompletion.\n
2	en	908	0x38c3b0	232507	58					59	C'mon, Boss. Let's get to that base!\n
2	en	909	0x38d5b0	232795	0					2	Snake, the Peace Walker platform and AI\nhave been shipped to the final testing\nbase.\n
2	en	909	0x38d5b0	232795	1					2	Once assembled, it's only a matter of\ntime before they launch the nukes. Hurry!\n
2	en	909	0x38d6f0	232815	0					1	Dammit, you've been spotted by the\nguards! Take them out before they take\nyou out!\n
